persönlichen Aufgaben","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js","Kompatibilität mit CLI","Unterstützung für mehrere parallele Agenten"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de tarefas diárias","Otimização do processo com ferramentas de IA","Utilização de agentes paralelos para aumentar a eficiência","Integração com tecnologias como React e Node.js","Suporte a CLI para automação de tarefas","Análise de dados para melhorar a tomada de decisões"],"ru":["Управление ежедневными задачами","Оптимизация процесса с помощью инструментов ИИ","Использование параллельных агентов для увеличения эффективности","Интеграция с технологиями seperti React и Node.js","Поддержка CLI для автоматизации задач","Анализ данных для улучшения принятия решений"],"ar":["ادارة المهام اليومية","تحسين العملية باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","استخدام وكلاء متوازي لزيادة الكفاءة","التكامل مع التكنولوجيا مثل React و Node.js","دعم CLI لتحسين المهام","تحليل البيانات لتحسين اتخاذ القرارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Dispatching Parallel Agents","日常燃尽图","个人任务优化","如何使用AI工具","AI工具安装","React","Python","Node.js"],"ja":["AIエージェント","並列エージェントのDispatcher","日々のバーンダウン","個人タスクの最適化","AIエージェントの使用方法","AIエージェントのインストール","React","Python","Node.js"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","병렬 에이전트 디스패처","일일 번다운","개인 작업의 최적화","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트 설치","React","Python","Node.js"],"es":["cómo usar agentes paralelos","herramientas de AI para tareas diarias","alternativas a agentes paralelos","agentes paralelos vs herramientas de automatización","instalación de agentes paralelos","guía de configuración de agentes paralelos","desarrollo de agentes paralelos con Python"],"fr":["comment utiliser des agents parallèles","outils d''IA pour tâches quotidiennes","alternatives aux agents parallèles","agents parallèles vs outils d''automatisation","installation d''agents parallèles","guide de configuration d''agents parallèles","développement d''agents parallèles avec Python"],"de":["wie man parallele Agenten verwendet","AI-Tools für tägliche Aufgaben","Alternativen zu parallelen Agenten","parallele Agenten vs Automatisierungstools","Installation von parallelen Agenten","Konfigurationsanleitung für parallele Agenten","Entwicklung von parallelen Agenten mit Python"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","dispatching de agentes paralelos","gerenciamento de tarefas","otimização de processo","react","node.js","cli","análise de dados","tomada de decisões"],"ru":["ии агенты","параллельное отправление","управление задачами","оптимизация процесса","react","node.js","cli","анализ данных","принятие решений"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","إرسال وكلاء متوازي","ادارة المهام","تحسين العملية","react","node.js","cli","تحليل البيانات","اتخاذ القرارات"]}},"owner":"bjconlan","repo":"burndown","repoPath":"bjconlan/burndown","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.916Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies","bodyPreview":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single","body":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single agent investigates all\" [shape=box];\n    \"One agent per problem domain\" [shape=box];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Sequential agents\" [shape=box];\n    \"Parallel dispatch\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Multiple failures?\" -> \"Are they independent?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Single agent investigates all\" [label=\"no - related\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Can they work in parallel?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Parallel dispatch\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Sequential agents\" [label=\"no - shared state\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- 3+ test files failing with different root causes\n- Multiple subsystems broken independently\n- Each problem can be understood without context from others\n- No shared state between investigations\n\n**Don''t use when:**\n- Failures are related (fix one might fix others)\n- Need to understand full system state\n- Agents would interfere with each other\n\n## The Pattern\n\n### 1. Identify Independent Domains\n\nGroup failures by what''s broken:\n- File A tests: Tool approval flow\n- File B tests: Batch completion behavior\n- File C tests: Abort functionality\n\nEach domain is independent - fixing tool approval doesn''t affect abort tests.\n\n### 2. Create Focused Agent Tasks\n\nEach agent gets:\n- **Specific scope:** One test file or subsystem\n- **Clear goal:** Make these tests pass\n- **Constraints:** Don''t change other code\n- **Expected output:** Summary of what you found and fixed\n\n### 3. Dispatch in Parallel\n\n```typescript\n// In Claude Code / AI environment\nTask(\"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts failures\")\n// All three run concurrently\n```\n\n### 4. Review and Integrate\n\nWhen agents return:\n- Read each summary\n- Verify fixes don''t conflict\n- Run full test suite\n- Integrate all changes\n\n## Agent Prompt Structure\n\nGood agent prompts are:\n1. **Focused** - One clear problem domain\n2. **Self-contained** - All context needed to understand the problem\n3. **Specific about output** - What should the agent return?\n\n```markdown\nFix the 3 failing tests in src/agents/agent-tool-abort.test.ts:\n\n1. \"should abort tool with partial output capture\" - expects ''interrupted at'' in message\n2. \"should handle mixed completed and aborted tools\" - fast tool aborted instead of completed\n3. \"should properly track pendingToolCount\" - expects 3 results but gets 0\n\nThese are timing/race condition issues. Your task:\n\n1. Read the test file and understand what each test verifies\n2. Identify root cause - timing issues or actual bugs?\n3. Fix by:\n   - Replacing arbitrary timeouts with event-based waiting\n   - Fixing bugs in abort implementation if found\n   - Adjusting test expectations if testing changed behavior\n\nDo NOT just increase timeouts - find the real issue.\n\nReturn: Summary of what you found and what you fixed.\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**❌ Too broad:** \"Fix all the tests\" - agent gets lost\n**✅ Specific:** \"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\" - focused scope\n\n**❌ No context:** \"Fix the race condition\" - agent doesn''t know where\n**✅ Context:** Paste the error messages and test names\n\n**❌ No constraints:** Agent might refactor everything\n**✅ Constraints:** \"Do NOT change production code\" or \"Fix tests only\"\n\n**❌ Vague output:** \"Fix it\" - you don''t know what changed\n**✅ Specific:** \"Return summary of root cause and changes\"\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n**Related failures:** Fixing one might fix others - investigate together first\n**Need full context:** Understanding requires seeing entire system\n**Exploratory debugging:** You don''t know what''s broken yet\n**Shared state:** Agents would interfere (editing same files, using same resources)\n\n## Real Example from Session\n\n**Scenario:** 6 test failures across 3 files after major refactoring\n\n**Failures:**\n- agent-tool-abort.test.ts: 3 failures (timing issues)\n- batch-completion-behavior.test.ts: 2 failures (tools not executing)\n- tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts: 1 failure (execution count = 0)\n\n**Decision:** Independent domains - abort logic separate from batch completion separate from race conditions\n\n**Dispatch:**\n```\nAgent 1 → Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\nAgent 2 → Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts\nAgent 3 → Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts\n```\n\n**Results:**\n- Agent 1: Replaced timeouts with event-based waiting\n- Agent 2: Fixed event structure bug (threadId in wrong place)\n- Agent 3: Added wait for async tool execution to complete\n\n**Integration:** All fixes independent, no conflicts, full suite green\n\n**Time saved:** 3 problems solved in parallel vs sequentially\n\n## Key Benefits\n\n1. **Parallelization** - Multiple investigations happen simultaneously\n2. **Focus** - Each agent has narrow scope, less context to track\n3. **Independence** - Agents don''t interfere with each other\n4. **Speed** - 3 problems solved in time of 1\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter agents return:\n1. **Review each summary** - Understand what changed\n2. **Check for conflicts** - Did agents edit same code?\n3. **Run full suite** - Verify all fixes work together\n4. **Spot check** - Agents can make systematic errors\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging session (2025-10-03):\n- 6 failures across 3 files\n- 3 agents dispatched in parallel\n- All investigations completed concurrently\n- All fixes integrated successfully\n- Zero conflicts between agent changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:02:55.994Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Tasking Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain needing concurrent problem-solving capabilities for independent tasks","zh":"适合于像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的多任务代理，需要同时处理独立任务的并发问题解决能力","ja":"AutoGPT や LangChain などのマルチタスクエージェントに適しており、独立したタスクの並行問題解決能力が必要","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 멀티태스킹 에이전트에 적합하며, 독립적인 태스크에 대한 병렬 문제 해결 능력이 필요","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Multi-Tarea como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades de resolución de problemas concurrentes para tareas independientes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de multitâche comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant des capacités de résolution de problèmes concurrentes pour des tâches indépendantes","de":"Ideal für Multi-Tasking-Agents wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die konkurrierende Problemlösungsfähigkeiten für unabhängige Aufgaben benötigen","pt":"Ideal para agentes de multi-tarefa como AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de capacidades de resolução de problemas concorrentes para tarefas independentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов с многозадачностью, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих возможностей параллельного решения проблем для независимых задач","ar":"مثالي لعميل التعدد مثل AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات حل المشكلات المتزامنة للأعمال المستقلة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dispatch parallel investigations for unrelated failures across different test files, subsystems, and bugs, utilizing daily burndowns for personal tasks and leveraging graph protocols like dot for visualization","zh":"赋予代理同时进行多个无关的故障调查的能力，利用日常燃尽图来跟踪个人任务，并利用图协议如 dot 进行可视化","ja":"エージェントに複数の無関係な故障を同時に調査する能力を与え、日常的なバーンダウンのために個人タスクを利用し、dot などのグラフプロトコルを使用して視覚化","ko":"에이전트가 여러 개의 무关한 오류를 동시에 조사할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 개인 작업을 위해 일일 번다운을 사용하고, dot과 같은 그래프 프로토콜을 사용하여 시각화","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones paralelas para fallos no relacionados en diferentes archivos de prueba, subsistemas y errores, utilizando quemados diarios para tareas personales y aprovechando protocolos gráficos como dot para la visualización","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des enquêtes parallèles pour des défaillances non liées dans différents fichiers de test, sous-systèmes et bogues, en utilisant des réductions quotidiennes pour les tâches personnelles et en exploitant des protocoles graphiques comme dot pour la visualisation","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, parallele Untersuchungen für nicht damit zusammenhängende Ausfälle in verschiedenen Testdateien, Subsystemen und Fehlern durchzuführen, indem sie tägliche Quellen für persönliche Aufgaben nutzen und Graphprotokolle wie dot für die Visualisierung nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a iniciar investigações paralelas para falhas não relacionadas em diferentes arquivos de teste, subsistemas e bugs, utilizando queimas diárias para tarefas pessoais e aproveitando protocolos gráficos como dot para visualização","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить параллельные расследования по несвязанным сбоям в различных тестовых файлах, подсистемах и ошибках, используя ежедневные бурдауны для личных задач и используя графические протоколы, такие как dot, для визуализации","ar":"تمكن العميل من إجراء تحقيقات متوازية لأخطاء غير متعلقة في ملفات اختبار مختلفة ونظم فرعية وعيوب، واستخدام الحرق اليومي للأعمال الشخصية وتحقيق بروتوكولات الرسم مثل dot للتصوير"},"useCases":{"en":["Investigating multiple unrelated failures concurrently","Automating daily burndowns for personal tasks","Visualizing independent problem domains using graph protocols"],"zh":["同时调查多个无关的故障","自动进行个人任务的日常燃尽图","使用图协议来可视化独立的问题域"],"ja":["複数の無関係な故障を同時に調査","個人タスクの日常的なバーンダウンの自動化","グラフプロトコルを使用した独立した問題ドメインの視覚化"],"ko":["여러 개의 무关한 오류를 동시에 조사","개인 작업의 일일 번다운 자동화","그래프 프로토콜을 사용한 독립적인 문제 도메인의 시각화"],"es":["Investigar múltiples fallos no relacionados de forma concurrente","Automatizar quemados diarios para tareas personales","Visualizar dominios de problemas independientes utilizando protocolos gráficos"],"fr":["Enquêter sur plusieurs défaillances non liées de manière concurrente","Automatiser les réductions quotidiennes pour les tâches personnelles","Visualiser des domaines de problèmes indépendants en utilisant des protocoles graphiques"],"de":["Mehrere nicht damit zusammenhängende Ausfälle gleichzeitig untersuchen","Tägliche Quellen für persönliche Aufgaben automatisieren","Unabhängige Problemdomänen unter Verwendung von Graphprotokollen visualisieren"],"pt":["Investigar várias falhas não relacionadas concorrentemente","Automatizar queimas diárias para tarefas pessoais","Visualizar domínios de problemas independentes usando protocolos gráficos"],"ru":["Расследование нескольких несвязанных сбойов одновременно","Автоматизация ежедневных бурдаунов для личных задач","Визуализация независимых проблемных доменов с помощью графических протоколов"],"ar":["تحقيق عدة أخطاء غير متعلقة في وقت واحد","تأتمتة الحرق اليومي للأعمال الشخصية","تصوير المجالات المستقلة للمشاكل باستخدام بروتوكولات الرسم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires independent problem domains","Limited to unrelated failures","Dependent on agent''s ability to handle concurrent tasks"],"zh":["需要独立的问题域","仅限于无关的故障","依赖于代理的并发任务处理能力"],"ja":["独立した問題ドメインが必要","無関係な故障のみに限定","エージェントの並行タスク処理能力に依存"],"ko":["독립적인 문제 도메인이 필요","무关한 오류만으로 제한","에이전트의 병렬 작업 처리 능력에 의존"],"es":["Requiere dominios de problemas independientes","Limitado a fallos no relacionados","Dependiente de la capacidad del agente para manejar tareas concurrentes"],"fr":["Nécessite des domaines de problèmes indépendants","Limité aux défaillances non liées","Dépend de la capacité de l''agent à gérer des tâches concurrentes"],"de":["Benötigt unabhängige Problemdomänen","Begrenzt auf nicht damit zusammenhängende Ausfälle","Abhängig von der Fähigkeit des Agents, konkurrierende Aufgaben zu verarbeiten"],"pt":["Exige domínios de problemas independentes","Limitado a falhas não relacionadas","Dependente da capacidade do agente de lidar com tarefas concorrentes"],"ru":["Требует независимых проблемных доменов","Ограничен несвязанными сбоями","Зависит от способности агента обрабатывать параллельные задачи"],"ar":["يتطلب مجالات مشاكل مستقلة","محدود بأخطاء غير متعلقة","يعتمد على قدرة العميل على التعامل مع المهام المتزامنة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c628917689ccc12ce9991615db6824d44c4fe71f8427cd959560aebe6a1a6476","qualityScore":46}');
