"de":["Terminal-Oberfläche für Anwendungen","Integration mit KI-Tools","Effizienz im Arbeitsablauf","Zugriff auf Anwendungs-Funktionen","Anpassung der Terminal-Oberfläche"],"pt":["Interface de terminal intuitiva","Acesso a todas as ferramentas em um só lugar","Gerenciamento eficiente de projetos","Integração com React, Python e Node.js","Suporte a CLI","Extensão de funcionalidades com plugins"],"ru":["Интуитивный терминальный интерфейс","Доступ ко всем инструментам в одном месте","Эффективное управление проектами","Интеграция с React, Python и Node.js","Поддержка CLI","Расширение функциональности с помощью плагинов"],"ar":["واجهة طرفية بديهية","الوصول إلى جميع الأدوات في مكان واحد","إدارة مشاريع فعالة","التكامل مع React و Python و Node.js","دعم CLI","توسيع الوظائف مع الإضافات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用新issue AI智能工具","新issue AI智能工具教程","基于终端的X应用开发","新issue AI智能工具与其他工具的比较","新issue AI智能工具安装指南","新issue AI智能工具设置教程"],"ja":["新規issue AIエージェントの使い方","新規issue AIエージェントのチュートリアル","TerminalベースのXアプリケーション開発","新規issue AIエージェントと他のツールの比較","新規issue AIエージェントのインストールガイド","新規issue AIエージェントの設定チュートリアル"],"ko":["새로운 이슈 AI 에이전트 사용 방법","새로운 이슈 AI 에이전트 튜토리얼","터미널 기반의 X 애플리케이션 개발","새로운 이슈 AI 에이전트와 다른 도구의 비교","새로운 이슈 AI 에이전트 설치 가이드","새로운 이슈 AI 에이전트 설정 튜토리얼"],"es":["herramientas de AI","interfaz de terminal","aplicaciones de desarrollo","flujo de trabajo eficiente","guias de instalación de new-issue","alternativas a new-issue","new-issue vs otras herramientas de AI","cómo utilizar new-issue","qué es new-issue"],"fr":["outils d''IA","interface de terminal","applications de développement","flux de travail efficace","guides d''installation de new-issue","alternatives à new-issue","new-issue vs autres outils d''IA","comment utiliser new-issue","qu''est-ce que new-issue"],"de":["KI-Tools","Terminal-Oberfläche","Entwicklungsanwendungen","effizienter Arbeitsablauf","Installationsanleitungen für new-issue","Alternativen zu new-issue","new-issue vs andere KI-Tools","wie man new-issue verwendet","was ist new-issue"],"pt":["como usar new-issue","o que é new-issue","alternativas para new-issue","new-issue vs outras ferramentas","instalar new-issue","guia de configuração do new-issue","desenvolvimento de aplicativos com new-issue","integrar new-issue com react","new-issue e python"],"ru":["как использовать new-issue","что такое new-issue","альтернативы new-issue","new-issue vs другие инструменты","установить new-issue","руководство по настройке new-issue","разработка приложений с new-issue","интегрировать new-issue с react","new-issue и python"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام new-issue","ما هو new-issue","بديلات ل new-issue","new-issue مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت new-issue","دليل إعداد new-issue","تطوير التطبيقات مع new-issue","دمج new-issue مع react","new-issue و python"]}},"owner":"ainergiz","repo":"xfeed","repoPath":"ainergiz/xfeed","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.927Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"new-issue","description":"Create GitHub issues with duplicate detection and codebase analysis. Use when you discover a bug, improvement, or issue that wasnt in the original scope/spec during development. Triggers on phrases like create an issue, file a bug, this should be tracked, we should fix this later, out of scope issue, noticed a problem, found a bug.","bodyPreview":"# Smart GitHub Issue Creation\n\nThis skill helps create well-researched GitHub issues while preventing duplicates and wasted effort.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- You discover a bug or issue that''s **outside the current task''s scope**\n- You notice something that should be fixed but isn''t part of the current spec\n- The user mentions wanting to \"track this for later\" or \"create an issue\"\n- You find an improvement opportunity while working on something else\n- The user expli","body":"# Smart GitHub Issue Creation\n\nThis skill helps create well-researched GitHub issues while preventing duplicates and wasted effort.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- You discover a bug or issue that''s **outside the current task''s scope**\n- You notice something that should be fixed but isn''t part of the current spec\n- The user mentions wanting to \"track this for later\" or \"create an issue\"\n- You find an improvement opportunity while working on something else\n- The user explicitly asks to create an issue or file a bug\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Clarify the Issue\n\nIf the issue description is vague or missing, ask the user:\n> \"What issue would you like to create? Describe the bug, feature, or improvement.\"\n\n### Step 2: Check if Already Fixed/Implemented\n\nBefore creating, verify this isn''t already solved:\n\n1. **Search codebase** for related keywords:\n   ```bash\n   # Use Grep/Glob to find relevant code\n   ```\n\n2. **Check recent commits** (filter by relevant keywords):\n   ```bash\n   # Generic recent commits\n   gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits --jq ''.[0:20] | .[] | \"\\(.sha[0:7]) \\(.commit.message | split(\"\\n\")[0])\"''\n\n   # Targeted search for specific keywords (more useful)\n   gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits --jq ''[.[] | select(.commit.message | test(\"KEYWORD1|KEYWORD2\"; \"i\"))] | .[0:10] | .[] | \"\\(.sha[0:7]) \\(.commit.message | split(\"\\n\")[0])\"''\n   ```\n   Replace `KEYWORD1|KEYWORD2` with terms relevant to the issue (e.g., \"retweet|repost\" for a retweet bug).\n\n3. **If already fixed/implemented**, inform the user:\n   > \"It looks like this might already be addressed. I found [what you found]. Are you aware of this?\"\n\n   Options: \"Show me the existing solution\", \"Create the issue anyway\", \"Cancel\"\n\n### Step 3: Check Existing GitHub Issues\n\nSearch for duplicates:\n\n1. **Search open issues:**\n   ```bash\n   gh issue list --state open --limit 50 --json number,title,body,labels,url\n   ```\n\n2. **Search closed issues:**\n   ```bash\n   gh issue list --state closed --limit 30 --json number,title,body,labels,url,closedAt\n   ```\n\n3. **Keyword search:**\n   ```bash\n   gh search issues --repo {owner}/{repo} \"keywords\" --limit 20 --json number,title,body,url,state\n   ```\n\n4. **Fetch details with comments for promising matches:**\n   ```bash\n   gh issue view <number> --json number,title,body,comments,labels,state\n   ```\n\n5. **Based on findings:**\n\n   **EXACT DUPLICATE:**\n   > \"I found an existing issue #[number] - [title] that matches this. What would you like to do?\"\n   - Options: \"Add comment to existing\", \"View details\", \"Create anyway\", \"Cancel\"\n\n   **RELATED ISSUE:**\n   > \"I found related issue #[number]. Your issue could be a comment, sub-issue, or separate. Preference?\"\n   - Options: \"Add as comment\", \"Create as sub-issue (I''ll activate gh-subissues skill)\", \"Create separate issue\"\n\n   **CLOSED ISSUE:**\n   > \"This was previously reported as #[number] and [fixed/rejected]. Context: [summary]. Still want to proceed?\"\n\n### Step 4: Research Potential Solutions\n\nIf you have enough context:\n\n1. **Explore codebase** for patterns and relevant files\n2. **Use web search** via Task tool for best practices\n3. **Formulate 1-3 approaches** with:\n   - Brief description\n   - Files that would need changes\n   - Trade-offs (if applicable)\n\n### Step 5: Draft Issue Content\n\nStructure the issue:\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\n[1-2 sentences]\n\n## Context\n[Background, how discovered, why it matters]\n\n## Current Behavior (for bugs)\n[What happens now]\n\n## Expected Behavior\n[What should happen]\n\n## Potential Implementation (optional)\n### Approach 1: [Name]\n- Description\n- Files: `path/to/file.ts`\n\n## Additional Context\n[Related issues, screenshots, etc.]\n```\n\n### Step 6: Confirm Before Creating\n\nPresent a **concise summary** (don''t overwhelm with details upfront):\n\n> \"Ready to create issue:\n>\n> **Title:** [title]\n> **Summary:** [1-2 sentences max]\n>\n> Does this look good?\"\n\nOptions: \"Create the issue\", \"Show more details\", \"Edit first\", \"Cancel\"\n\n**If user selects \"Show more details\"**, then display:\n- Key findings from codebase exploration\n- Proposed implementation approaches\n- Files that would be affected\n\n### Step 7: Create the Issue\n\n```bash\ngh issue create --title \"type(area): description\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n[structured content]\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nThen display the URL and issue number.\n\n## Sub-Issue Support\n\nTo create as a sub-issue, say:\n> \"I''ll activate the gh-subissues skill to create this as a sub-issue of #[parent].\"\n\nThen use the Skill tool to invoke `gh-subissues`.\n\n## During Development: Out-of-Scope Issues\n\nWhen you notice an issue while working on something else:\n\n1. **Briefly mention it** to the user:\n   > \"While working on [current task], I noticed [issue]. This seems out of scope for the current work. Would you like me to create an issue to track this for later?\"\n\n2. **If user agrees**, run through this workflow\n3. **If user declines**, continue with the current task\n\nThis prevents scope creep while ensuring important issues aren''t forgotten.\n\n## Issue Title Conventions\n\nUse conventional format:\n- `fix(area): brief description` - Bug fixes\n- `feat(area): brief description` - New features\n- `refactor(area): brief description` - Code improvements\n- `docs(area): brief description` - Documentation\n- `chore(area): brief description` - Maintenance\n\n## Handling Screenshots & Attachments\n\nIf the user provides screenshots or images for the issue:\n\n1. **Check for attached files** in the conversation (e.g., `.context/attachments/`)\n2. **Read and understand** the images before drafting the issue\n3. **Create the issue first** (without images or with placeholder text) to get the issue number\n4. **Upload images with issue-prefixed names** to a draft release:\n\n```bash\n# Create or reuse a draft release for issue assets\ngh release view issue-assets 2>/dev/null || \\\n  gh release create issue-assets --draft --title \"Issue Assets\" --notes \"Screenshots for issues\"\n\n# Copy and rename with issue prefix (e.g., 216-description.png)\ncp \"path/to/screenshot.png\" /tmp/{issue#}-{description}.png\n\n# Upload the renamed file\ngh release upload issue-assets /tmp/{issue#}-{description}.png\n\n# Get the URL\ngh release view issue-assets --json assets --jq ''.assets[] | select(.name | startswith(\"{issue#}\")) | \"\\(.name): \\(.url)\"''\n```\n\n5. **Edit the issue** to add the image URLs (not as a separate comment):\n```bash\ngh issue edit {issue#} --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n[issue body with images]\n![description](https://github.com/owner/repo/releases/download/issue-assets/{issue#}-description.png)\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n**Naming convention:** `{issue#}-{description}.png` (e.g., `216-xfeed-display.png`, `216-xcom-expected.png`)\n\n**Note:** The `gh` CLI cannot upload images directly to issues ([feature requested since 2020](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1895)). Release assets are the cleanest workaround that keeps images within the repo''s GitHub ecosystem.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Always prioritize preventing duplicates - saves everyone time\n- Be thorough but concise - don''t overwhelm the user\n- For simple, clearly new issues, streamline the process\n- Keep the user informed at each decision point\n- Check for user-provided debug URLs and include them in the issue\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:05:57.437Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Assistants needing streamlined GitHub issue creation and duplicate prevention.","zh":"非常适合需要简化 GitHub 问题创建和防止重复的开发助手。","ja":"GitHub の問題作成をストリームライン化し、重複を防ぐ必要がある開発アシスタントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub 이슈 생성과 중복 방지를 간소화해야 하는 개발 어시스턴트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para asistentes de desarrollo que necesitan una creación de problemas de GitHub optimizada y prevención de duplicados.","fr":"Idéal pour les assistants de développement ayant besoin d''une création de problèmes GitHub rationalisée et d''une prévention des doublons.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsassistenten, die eine optimierte GitHub-Problemerstellung und Duplikatvermeidung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Assistente de Desenvolvimento que precisa de criação de problemas do GitHub simplificada e prevenção de duplicatas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для помощников разработки, которым необходима упрощенная создания проблем GitHub и предотвращение дубликатов.","ar":"مثالي لمساعدي التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء مشاكل GitHub مبسطة ومنع التكرارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create well-researched GitHub issues using terminal-based interfaces, preventing duplicates and wasted effort through comprehensive content analysis and smart issue tracking, leveraging protocols like GitHub API and file formats like Markdown.","zh":"使代理能够使用基于终端的接口创建经过深入研究的 GitHub 问题，通过全面内容分析和智能问题跟踪防止重复和浪费精力，利用 GitHub API 和 Markdown 等文件格式等协议。","ja":"エージェントがターミナルベースのインターフェイスを使用して徹底的な調査を行った GitHub の問題を作成できるようにし、GitHub API や Markdown などのプロトコルを利用して重複や無駄な労力を防ぐことで、包括的なコンテンツ分析とスマートな問題追跡を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 터미널 기반 인터페이스를 사용하여 철저히 조사된 GitHub 이슈를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, GitHub API 및 Markdown와 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여 중복 및 불필요한 노력을 방지함으로써 포괄적인 콘텐츠 분석 및 스마트 이슈 추적을 통해 에이전트를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear problemas de GitHub bien investigados utilizando interfaces basadas en terminal, evitando duplicados y esfuerzo desperdiciado a través de un análisis de contenido integral y un seguimiento inteligente de problemas, aprovechando protocolos como GitHub API y formatos de archivo como Markdown.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des problèmes GitHub bien étudiés en utilisant des interfaces basées sur le terminal, évitant les doublons et les efforts gaspillés grâce à une analyse de contenu complète et à un suivi intelligent des problèmes, en exploitant des protocoles comme GitHub API et des formats de fichiers comme Markdown.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, gut recherchierte GitHub-Probleme mithilfe von terminalbasierten Schnittstellen zu erstellen, wodurch Duplikate und verschwendete Anstrengung durch umfassende Inhaltsanalyse und intelligente Problemmeldung verhindert werden, indem Protokolle wie GitHub API und Dateiformate wie Markdown genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar problemas do GitHub bem pesquisados usando interfaces baseadas em terminal, evitando duplicatas e esforço desperdiçado por meio da análise abrangente de conteúdo e acompanhamento inteligente de problemas, aproveitando protocolos como GitHub API e formatos de arquivo como Markdown.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать хорошо исследованные проблемы GitHub с использованием терминальных интерфейсов, предотвращая дубликаты и потраченные усилия посредством комплексного анализа содержания и умного отслеживания проблем, используя протоколы типа GitHub API и форматы файлов типа Markdown.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء مشاكل GitHub مدروسة جيدًا باستخدام واجهات المستخدم القائمة على الطرفية، وتجنب التكرارات والجهد المهدور من خلال تحليل المحتوى الشامل وتتبع ذكي للمشاكل، مستفِدًا من بروتوكولات مثل GitHub API وأشكال الملفات مثل Markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating bug tracking","Generating improvement opportunities","Preventing duplicate issues"],"zh":["自动化缺陷跟踪","生成改进机会","防止重复问题"],"ja":["バグトラッキングの自動化","改善の機会の生成","重複問題の防止"],"ko":["버그 추적 자동화","개선 기회의 생성","중복 이슈 방지"],"es":["Automatización de seguimiento de errores","Generación de oportunidades de mejora","Prevención de problemas duplicados"],"fr":["Automatisation de la surveillance des bogues","Génération d''opportunités d''amélioration","Prévention de problèmes en double"],"de":["Automatisierung der Fehlerverfolgung","Generierung von Verbesserungsmöglichkeiten","Verhinderung von doppelten Problemen"],"pt":["Automatização de rastreamento de bugs","Geração de oportunidades de melhoria","Prevenção de problemas duplicados"],"ru":["Автоматизация отслеживания ошибок","Генерация возможностей улучшения","Предотвращение дубликатов проблем"],"ar":["أتمتة تتبع الأخطاء","توليد فرص للتحسين","منع المشاكل المكررة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub API access","Terminal-based interface only","Limited to GitHub issues"],"zh":["需要 GitHub API 访问","仅限终端界面","仅限 GitHub 问题"],"ja":["GitHub API アクセスが必要","ターミナルベースのインターフェイスのみ","GitHub の問題のみ"],"ko":["GitHub API 접근 필요","터미널 기반 인터페이스만","GitHub 이슈만"],"es":["Requiere acceso a GitHub API","Interfaz basada en terminal solo","Limitado a problemas de GitHub"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à GitHub API","Interface basée sur le terminal uniquement","Limité aux problèmes GitHub"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf GitHub API","Nur terminalbasierte Schnittstelle","Begrenzt auf GitHub-Probleme"],"pt":["Requer acesso à GitHub API","Interface baseada em terminal apenas","Limitado a problemas do GitHub"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к GitHub API","Только терминальный интерфейс","Ограничен до проблем GitHub"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى GitHub API","واجهة الطرفية فقط","محدود لمشاكل GitHub"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"1cbafc7994897da52899011b9091ef8ec6d0a1502be46322a8539242ea64baa8","qualityScore":46}');
