код في JavaScript","en":"quality-scan"},"description":{"zh":"质量扫描JavaScript SDK为Socket.dev API提供安全可靠的AI智能代理解决方案","ja":"Quality ScanのJavaScript SDKは、Socket.dev APIのためのセキュアで信頼性の高いAIエージェントソリューションを提供します","ko":"품질 스캔의 JavaScript SDK는 Socket.dev API를 위한 보안하고 안정적인 AI 에이전트 솔루션을 제공합니다","es":"El SDK de JavaScript para Socket.dev API es una herramienta de inteligencia artificial para mejorar la seguridad de tus aplicaciones","fr":"Le SDK JavaScript pour Socket.dev API est un outil d''intelligence artificielle pour améliorer la sécurité de vos applications","de":"Das JavaScript-SDK für Socket.dev API ist ein KI-Tool zur Verbesserung der Sicherheit Ihrer Anwendungen","pt":"O Quality-Scan é uma ferramenta de análise de código em JavaScript que ajuda a melhorar a qualidade do seu código.","ru":"Quality-Scan - это инструмент для анализа кода в JavaScript, который помогает улучшить качество вашего кода.","ar":"Quality-Scan هو أداة تحليل код في JavaScript التي تساعد في تحسين جودةコード.","en":"JavaScript SDK for Socket.dev API"},"definition":{"en":"JavaScript SDK for Socket.dev API"},"features":{"zh":["安全性检查","可靠性检查","JavaScript SDK集成","Socket.dev API支持","Typescript支持"],"ja":["セキュリティチェック","信頼性チェック","JavaScript SDK統合","Socket.dev APIサポート","Typescriptサポート"],"ko":["보안성 확인","안정성 확인","JavaScript SDK 통합","Socket.dev API 지원","Typescript 지원"],"es":["Análisis de calidad de código","Detección de vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Integración con Socket.dev API","Compatibilidad con JavaScript y TypeScript","Mejora de la seguridad de las aplicaciones"],"fr":["Analyse de la qualité du code","Détection des vulnérabilités de sécurité","Intégration avec Socket.dev API","Compatibilité avec JavaScript et TypeScript","Amélioration de la sécurité des applications"],"de":["Code-Qualitätsanalyse","Erkennung von Sicherheitslücken","Integration mit Socket.dev API","Kompatibilität mit JavaScript und TypeScript","Verbesserung der Sicherheit von Anwendungen"],"pt":["Análise de código em JavaScript","Identificação de problemas de segurança e performance","Suporte a SDKs em JavaScript","Integração com Socket.dev API"],"ru":["Анализ кода в JavaScript","Выявление проблем безопасности и производительности","Поддержка SDKs в JavaScript","Интеграция с Socket.dev API"],"ar":["تحليل код في JavaScript","تحديد مشاكل أمنية و性能","دعم SDKs في JavaScript","تеграção مع Socket.dev API"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用质量扫描","什么是AI智能代理","Socket.dev API替代品","质量扫描与安全性","JavaScript SDK安装","质量扫描设置指南","AI智能代理安全性","Socket.dev API文档"],"ja":["品質スキャンの使用方法","AIエージェントとは","Socket.dev APIの代替","品質スキャンとセキュリティ","JavaScript SDKのインストール","品質スキャンの設定ガイド","AIエージェントのセキュリティ","Socket.dev APIのドキュメント"],"ko":["품질 스캔 사용 방법","AI 에이전트란","Socket.dev API 대체","품질 스캔과 보안","JavaScript SDK 설치","품질 스캔 설정 가이드","AI 에이전트 보안","Socket.dev API 문서"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","SDK de JavaScript","Socket.dev API","seguridad de aplicaciones","cómo usar Socket.dev API","alternativas a Socket.dev API","instalación de Socket.dev API"],"fr":["outils d''intelligence artificielle","SDK JavaScript","Socket.dev API","sécurité des applications","comment utiliser Socket.dev API","alternatives à Socket.dev API","installation de Socket.dev API"],"de":["KI-Tools","JavaScript-SDK","Socket.dev API","Sicherheit von Anwendungen","wie man Socket.dev API verwendet","Alternativen zu Socket.dev API","Installation von Socket.dev API"],"pt":["quality-scan","análise de código","segurança de código","performance de código","javascript","sdk","socket.dev"],"ru":["quality-scan","анализ кода","безопасность кода","производительность кода","javascript","sdk","socket.dev"],"ar":["quality-scan","تحليل код","أمانية код","performance de código","javascript","sdk","socket.dev"]}},"owner":"SocketDev","repo":"socket-sdk-js","repoPath":"SocketDev/socket-sdk-js","stars":44,"forks":15,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T19:28:14Z","topics":["api","javascript","sdk","security","socket","typescript"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"quality-scan","description":"Updates dependencies, cleans up junk files, and performs comprehensive quality scans across codebase to identify critical bugs, logic errors, and workflow problems. Spawns specialized agents for targeted analysis and generates prioritized improvement tasks. Use when improving code quality, before releases, or investigating issues.","bodyPreview":"# quality-scan\n\n<task>\nYour task is to perform comprehensive quality scans across the socket-sdk-js codebase using specialized agents to identify critical bugs, logic errors, and workflow problems. Before scanning, update dependencies and clean up junk files to ensure a clean and organized repository. Generate a prioritized report with actionable improvement tasks.\n</task>\n\n<context>\n**What is Quality Scanning?**\nQuality scanning uses specialized AI agents to systematically analyze code for diff","body":"# quality-scan\n\n<task>\nYour task is to perform comprehensive quality scans across the socket-sdk-js codebase using specialized agents to identify critical bugs, logic errors, and workflow problems. Before scanning, update dependencies and clean up junk files to ensure a clean and organized repository. Generate a prioritized report with actionable improvement tasks.\n</task>\n\n<context>\n**What is Quality Scanning?**\nQuality scanning uses specialized AI agents to systematically analyze code for different categories of issues. Each agent type focuses on specific problem domains and reports findings with severity levels and actionable fixes.\n\n**socket-sdk-js Architecture:**\nThis is Socket Security''s TypeScript/JavaScript SDK that:\n- Provides programmatic access to Socket.dev security analysis\n- Implements HTTP client with retry logic and rate limiting\n- Handles API authentication and request/response validation\n- Generates strict TypeScript types from OpenAPI specifications\n- Supports package scanning, SBOM generation, and organization management\n- Implements comprehensive test coverage with Vitest\n\n**Scan Types Available:**\n1. **critical** - Crashes, security vulnerabilities, resource leaks, data corruption\n2. **logic** - Algorithm errors, edge cases, type guards, off-by-one errors\n3. **workflow** - Build scripts, CI issues, cross-platform compatibility\n4. **security** - GitHub Actions workflow security (zizmor scanner)\n5. **documentation** - README accuracy, outdated docs, missing documentation\n\n**Why Quality Scanning Matters:**\n- Catches bugs before they reach production\n- Identifies security vulnerabilities early\n- Improves code quality systematically\n- Provides actionable fixes with file:line references\n- Prioritizes issues by severity for efficient remediation\n- Keeps dependencies up-to-date\n- Cleans up junk files for a well-organized repository\n\n**Agent Prompts:**\nAll agent prompts are embedded in `reference.md` with structured <context>, <instructions>, <pattern>, and <output_format> tags following Claude best practices.\n</context>\n\n<constraints>\n**CRITICAL Requirements:**\n- Read-only analysis (no code changes during scan)\n- Must complete all enabled scans before reporting\n- Findings must be prioritized by severity (Critical → High → Medium → Low)\n- Must generate actionable tasks with file:line references\n- All findings must include suggested fixes\n\n**Do NOT:**\n- Fix issues during scan (analysis only - report findings)\n- Skip critical scan types without user permission\n- Report findings without file/line references\n- Proceed if codebase has uncommitted changes (warn but continue)\n\n**Do ONLY:**\n- Update dependencies before scanning\n- Run enabled scan types in priority order (critical → logic → workflow)\n- Generate structured findings with severity levels\n- Provide actionable improvement tasks with specific code changes\n- Report statistics and coverage metrics\n- Deduplicate findings across scans\n</constraints>\n\n<instructions>\n\n## Process\n\nExecute the following phases sequentially to perform comprehensive quality analysis.\n\n### Phase 1: Validate Environment\n\n<prerequisites>\nVerify the environment before starting scans:\n</prerequisites>\n\n```bash\ngit status\n```\n\n<validation>\n**Expected State:**\n- Working directory should be clean (warn if dirty but continue)\n- On a valid branch\n- Node modules installed\n\n**If working directory dirty:**\n- Warn user: \"Working directory has uncommitted changes - continuing with scan\"\n- Continue with scans (quality scanning is read-only)\n\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Update Dependencies\n\n<action>\nUpdate dependencies across Socket Security SDK repositories to ensure latest versions:\n</action>\n\n**Target Repositories:**\n1. **socket-sdk-js** (current repository)\n2. **socket-cli** (`../socket-cli/`)\n3. **socket-btm** (`../socket-btm/`)\n4. **socket-registry** (`../socket-registry/`)\n\n**Update Process:**\n\nFor each repository, run dependency updates:\n\n```bash\n# socket-sdk-js (current repo)\npnpm run update\n\n# socket-cli\ncd ../socket-cli && pnpm run update && cd -\n\n# socket-btm\ncd ../socket-btm && pnpm run update && cd -\n\n# socket-registry\ncd ../socket-registry && pnpm run update && cd -\n```\n\n<validation>\n**For each repository:**\n1. Check if directory exists (skip if not found)\n2. Run `pnpm run update` command\n3. Report success or failure\n4. Track updated packages count\n5. Continue even if some repos fail\n\n**Expected Results:**\n- Dependencies updated in available repositories\n- Report number of packages updated per repository\n- Note any repositories that were skipped (not found)\n- Continue with scan even if updates fail\n\n**Track for reporting:**\n- Repositories updated: N/4\n- Total packages updated: N\n- Failed updates: N (continue with warnings)\n- Skipped repositories: [list]\n\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Repository Cleanup\n\n<action>\nClean up junk files and organize the repository before scanning:\n</action>\n\n**Cleanup Tasks:**\n\n1. **Remove SCREAMING_TEXT.md files** (all-caps .md files) that are NOT:\n   - Inside `.claude/` directory\n   - Inside `docs/` directory\n   - Named `README.md`, `LICENSE`, or `SECURITY.md`\n\n2. **Remove temporary test files** in wrong locations:\n   - `.test.mjs` or `.test.mts` files outside `test/` or `__tests__/` directories\n   - Temp files: `*.tmp`, `*.temp`, `.DS_Store`, `Thumbs.db`\n   - Editor backups: `*~`, `*.swp`, `*.swo`, `*.bak`\n   - Test artifacts: `*.log` files in root or package directories (not logs/)\n\n```bash\n# Find SCREAMING_TEXT.md files (all caps with .md extension)\nfind . -type f -name ''*.md'' \\\n  ! -path ''./.claude/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''./docs/*'' \\\n  ! -name ''README.md'' \\\n  ! -name ''LICENSE'' \\\n  ! -name ''SECURITY.md'' \\\n  | grep -E ''/[A-Z_]+\\.md$''\n\n# Find test files in wrong locations\nfind . -type f \\( -name ''*.test.mjs'' -o -name ''*.test.mts'' \\) \\\n  ! -path ''*/test/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/__tests__/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/node_modules/*''\n\n# Find temp files\nfind . -type f \\( \\\n  -name ''*.tmp'' -o \\\n  -name ''*.temp'' -o \\\n  -name ''.DS_Store'' -o \\\n  -name ''Thumbs.db'' -o \\\n  -name ''*~'' -o \\\n  -name ''*.swp'' -o \\\n  -name ''*.swo'' -o \\\n  -name ''*.bak'' \\\n\\) ! -path ''*/node_modules/*''\n\n# Find log files in wrong places (not in logs/ or build/ directories)\nfind . -type f -name ''*.log'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/logs/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/build/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/node_modules/*'' \\\n  ! -path ''*/.git/*''\n```\n\n<validation>\n**For each file found:**\n1. Show the file path to user\n2. Explain why it''s considered junk\n3. Ask user for confirmation before deleting (use AskUserQuestion)\n4. Delete confirmed files: `git rm` if tracked, `rm` if untracked\n5. Report files removed\n\n**If no junk files found:**\n- Report: \"✓ Repository is clean - no junk files found\"\n\n**Important:**\n- Always get user confirmation before deleting\n- Show file contents if user is unsure\n- Track deleted files for reporting\n\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Determine Scan Scope\n\n<action>\nAsk user which scans to run:\n</action>\n\n**Default Scan Types** (run all unless user specifies):\n1. **critical** - Critical bugs (crashes, security, resource leaks)\n2. **logic** - Logic errors (algorithms, edge cases, type guards)\n3. **workflow** - Workflow problems (scripts, CI, git hooks)\n4. **security** - GitHub Actions security (template injection, cache poisoning, etc.)\n5. **documentation** - Documentation accuracy (README errors, outdated docs)\n\n**User Interaction:**\nUse AskUserQuestion tool:\n- Question: \"Which quality scans would you like to run?\"\n- Header: \"Scan Types\"\n- multiSelect: true\n- Options:\n  - \"All scans (recommended)\" → Run all scan types\n  - \"Critical only\" → Run critical scan only\n  - \"Critical + Logic\" → Run critical and logic scans\n  - \"Custom selection\" → Ask user to specify which scans\n\n**Default:** If user doesn''t specify, run all scans.\n\n<validation>\nValidate selected scan types exist in reference.md:\n- critical-scan → reference.md line ~5\n- logic-scan → reference.md line ~100\n- workflow-scan → reference.md line ~300\n- security-scan → reference.md line ~400\n- documentation-scan → reference.md line ~810\n\nIf user requests non-existent scan type, report error and suggest valid types.\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: Execute Scans\n\n<action>\nFor each enabled scan type, spawn a specialized agent using Task tool:\n</action>\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Critical scan\nTask({\n  subagent_type: \"general-purpose\",\n  description: \"Critical bugs scan\",\n  prompt: `${CRITICAL_SCAN_PROMPT_FROM_REFERENCE_MD}\n\nFocus on src/ directory (HTTP client, SDK class, type generation scripts).\n\nSDK-specific patterns to check:\n- HTTP client error handling (src/http-client.ts)\n- API method validation (src/socket-sdk-class.ts)\n- Type generation scripts (scripts/generate-*.mjs)\n- Promise handling and retry logic\n- JSON parsing errors\n- Rate limiting and timeout handling\n\nReport findings in this format:\n- File: path/to/file.ts:lineNumber\n- Issue: Brief description\n- Severity: Critical/High/Medium/Low\n- Pattern: Code snippet\n- Trigger: What input triggers this\n- Fix: Suggested fix\n- Impact: What happens if triggered\n\nScan systematically and report all findings. If no issues found, state that explicitly.`\n})\n```\n\n**For each scan:**\n1. Load agent prompt template from `reference.md`\n2. Customize for socket-sdk-js context (focus on src/, scripts/, test/)\n3. Spawn agent with Task tool using \"general-purpose\" subagent_type\n4. Capture findings from agent response\n5. Parse and categorize results\n\n**Execution Order:** Run scans sequentially in priority order:\n- critical (highest priority)\n- logic\n- workflow\n- security\n- documentation (lowest priority)\n\n**Agent Prompt Sources:**\n- Critical scan: reference.md starting at line ~12\n- Logic scan: reference.md starting at line ~100\n- Workflow scan: reference.md starting at line ~300\n- Security scan: reference.md starting at line ~400\n- Documentation scan: reference.md starting at line ~810\n\n<validation>\n**Structured Output Validation:**\n\nAfter each agent returns, validate output structure before parsing:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Verify agent completed successfully\nif [ -z \"\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: Agent returned no output\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# 2. Check for findings or clean report\nif ! echo \"\" | grep -qE ''(File:.*Issue:|No .* issues found|✓ Clean)''; then\n  echo \"WARNING: Agent output missing expected format\"\n  echo \"Agent may have encountered an error or found no issues\"\nfi\n\n# 3. Verify severity levels if findings exist\nif echo \"\" | grep -q \"File:\"; then\n  if ! echo \"\" | grep -qE ''Severity: (Critical|High|Medium|Low)''; then\n    echo \"WARNING: Findings missing severity classification\"\n  fi\nfi\n\n# 4. Verify fix suggestions if findings exist\nif echo \"\" | grep -q \"File:\"; then\n  if ! echo \"\" | grep -q \"Fix:\"; then\n    echo \"WARNING: Findings missing suggested fixes\"\n  fi\nfi\n```\n\n**Manual Verification Checklist:**\n- [ ] Agent output includes findings OR explicit \"No issues found\" statement\n- [ ] All findings include file:line references\n- [ ] All findings include severity level (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n- [ ] All findings include suggested fixes\n- [ ] Agent output is parseable and structured\n\n**For each scan completion:**\n- Verify agent completed without errors\n- Extract findings from agent output (or confirm \"No issues found\")\n- Parse into structured format (file, issue, severity, fix)\n- Track scan coverage (files analyzed)\n- Log any validation warnings for debugging\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 6: Aggregate Findings\n\n<action>\nCollect all findings from agents and aggregate:\n</action>\n\n```typescript\ninterface Finding {\n  file: string           // \"src/http-client.ts:89\"\n  issue: string          // \"Potential null pointer access\"\n  severity: \"Critical\" | \"High\" | \"Medium\" | \"Low\"\n  scanType: string       // \"critical\"\n  pattern: string        // Code snippet showing the issue\n  trigger: string        // What causes this issue\n  fix: string            // Suggested code change\n  impact: string         // What happens if triggered\n}\n```\n\n**Deduplication:**\n- Remove duplicate findings across scans (same file:line, same issue)\n- Keep the finding from the highest priority scan\n- Track which scans found the same issue\n\n**Prioritization:**\n- Sort by severity: Critical → High → Medium → Low\n- Within same severity, sort by scanType priority\n- Within same severity+scanType, sort alphabetically by file path\n\n<validation>\n**Checkpoint:** Verify aggregation:\n- Total findings count\n- Breakdown by severity (N critical, N high, N medium, N low)\n- Breakdown by scan type\n- Duplicate removal count (if any)\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 7: Generate Report\n\n<action>\nCreate structured quality report with all findings:\n</action>\n\n```markdown\n# Quality Scan Report\n\n**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD\n**Repository:** socket-sdk-js\n**Scans:** [list of scan types run]\n**Files Scanned:** N\n**Findings:** N critical, N high, N medium, N low\n\n## Critical Issues (Priority 1) - N found\n\n### src/http-client.ts:89\n- **Issue**: Potential null pointer access in retry logic\n- **Pattern**: `const result = response.data.items[0]`\n- **Trigger**: When API returns empty array\n- **Fix**: `const items = response.data?.items ?? []; if (items.length === 0) throw new Error(''No items found''); const result = items[0]`\n- **Impact**: Crashes SDK, breaks user applications\n- **Scan**: critical\n\n## High Issues (Priority 2) - N found\n\n[Similar format for high severity issues]\n\n## Medium Issues (Priority 3) - N found\n\n[Similar format for medium severity issues]\n\n## Low Issues (Priority 4) - N found\n\n[Similar format for low severity issues]\n\n## Scan Coverage\n\n- **Critical scan**: N files analyzed in src/, scripts/\n- **Logic scan**: N files analyzed (API methods, type generation)\n- **Workflow scan**: N files analyzed (package.json, scripts/, .github/)\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. Address N critical issues immediately before next release\n2. Review N high-severity logic errors in HTTP client\n3. Schedule N medium issues for next sprint\n4. Low-priority items can be addressed during refactoring\n\n## No Findings\n\n[If a scan found no issues, list it here:]\n- Critical scan: ✓ Clean\n- Logic scan: ✓ Clean\n```\n\n**Output Report:**\n1. Display report to console (user sees it)\n2. Offer to save to file (optional): `reports/quality-scan-YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n\n<validation>\n**Report Quality Checks:**\n- All findings include file:line references\n- All findings include suggested fixes\n- Findings are grouped by severity\n- Scan coverage statistics included\n- Recommendations are actionable\n</validation>\n\n---\n\n### Phase 8: Complete\n\n<completion_signal>\n```xml\n<promise>QUALITY_SCAN_COMPLETE</promise>\n```\n</completion_signal>\n\n<summary>\nReport these final metrics to the user:\n\n**Quality Scan Complete**\n========================\n✓ Dependency updates: N repositories, N packages updated\n✓ Repository cleanup: N junk files removed\n✓ Scans completed: [list of scan types]\n✓ Total findings: N (N critical, N high, N medium, N low)\n✓ Files scanned: N\n✓ Report generated: Yes\n✓ Scan duration: [calculated from start to end]\n\n**Dependency Update Summary:**\n- socket-sdk-js: N packages updated\n- socket-cli: N packages updated (or skipped)\n- socket-btm: N packages updated (or skipped)\n- socket-registry: N packages updated (or skipped)\n\n**Repository Cleanup Summary:**\n- SCREAMING_TEXT.md files removed: N\n- Temporary test files removed: N\n- Temp/backup files removed: N\n- Log files cleaned up: N\n\n**Critical Issues Requiring Immediate Attention:**\n- N critical issues found\n- Review report above for details and fixes\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1. Address critical issues immediately\n2. Review high-severity findings\n3. Schedule medium/low issues appropriately\n4. Re-run scans after fixes to verify\n\nAll findings include file:line references and suggested fixes.\n</summary>\n\n</instructions>\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- ✅ `<promise>QUALITY_SCAN_COMPLETE</promise>` output\n- ✅ Dependencies updated in available repositories\n- ✅ All enabled scans completed without errors\n- ✅ Findings prioritized by severity (Critical → Low)\n- ✅ All findings include file:line references\n- ✅ Actionable suggestions provided for all findings\n- ✅ Report generated with statistics and coverage metrics\n- ✅ Duplicate findings removed\n\n## Scan Types\n\nSee `reference.md` for detailed agent prompts with structured tags:\n\n- **critical-scan** - Null access, promise rejections, race conditions, resource leaks\n- **logic-scan** - Off-by-one errors, type guards, edge cases, algorithm correctness\n- **workflow-scan** - Scripts, package.json, git hooks, CI configuration\n- **security-scan** - GitHub Actions workflow security (runs zizmor scanner)\n- **documentation-scan** - README accuracy, outdated examples, incorrect package names, missing documentation\n\nAll agent prompts follow Claude best practices with <context>, <instructions>, <pattern>, <output_format>, and <quality_guidelines> tags.\n\n## Commands\n\nThis skill is self-contained. No external commands needed.\n\n## Context\n\nThis skill provides systematic code quality analysis for socket-sdk-js by:\n- Updating dependencies before scanning to ensure latest versions\n- Spawning specialized agents for targeted analysis\n- Using Task tool to run agents autonomously\n- Embedding agent prompts in reference.md following best practices\n- Generating prioritized, actionable reports\n- Supporting partial scans (user can select specific scan types)\n\nFor detailed agent prompts with best practices structure, see `reference.md`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:30:28.171Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced JavaScript analysis and Socket.dev API integration capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级JavaScript分析和Socket.dev API集成能力的代码审查代理。","ja":"JavaScriptの高度な分析とSocket.dev APIの統合機能が必要なコードレビューエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 JavaScript 분석 및 Socket.dev API 통합 기능이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan análisis de JavaScript avanzado y capacidades de integración de la API de Socket.dev.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une analyse JavaScript avancée et des capacités d''intégration de l''API Socket.dev.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die erweiterte JavaScript-Analyse und Socket.dev-API-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise avançada de JavaScript e capacidades de integração da API Socket.dev.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа JavaScript и интеграции с API Socket.dev.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة الكود التي تحتاج إلى تحليل متقدم JavaScript و إمكانيات التكامل API Socket.dev."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive quality scans across codebases using the Socket.dev API and JavaScript SDK, identifying critical bugs, logic errors, and workflow problems through specialized agents, while utilizing dependencies like socket-sdk-js and generating prioritized reports with actionable improvement tasks.","zh":"赋予代理在整个代码库中使用Socket.dev API和JavaScript SDK执行全面质量扫描的能力，通过专业代理识别关键错误、逻辑错误和工作流问题，同时利用依赖项如socket-sdk-js，并生成优先的改进任务报告。","ja":"Socket.dev APIとJavaScript SDKを使用してコードベース全体で包括的な品質スキャンを実行するエージェントを可能にし、専門エージェントを通じて重要なバグ、論理エラー、ワークフローの問題を識別し、socket-sdk-jsなどの依存関係を利用して、優先度の付いた改善タスクのレポートを生成します。","ko":"Socket.dev API와 JavaScript SDK를 사용하여 코드베이스 전체에서 종합적인 품질 스캔을 수행할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여, 전문 에이전트를 통해 중요한 버그, 논리 오류 및 워크플로우 문제를 식별하고, socket-sdk-js와 같은 종속성을 사용하여 우선 순위가 지정된 개선 작업 레ポート를 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar análisis de calidad exhaustivos en codebases utilizando la API de Socket.dev y el SDK de JavaScript, identificando errores críticos, errores de lógica y problemas de flujo de trabajo a través de agentes especializados, mientras utiliza dependencias como socket-sdk-js y genera informes prioritizados con tareas de mejora accionables.","fr":"Autorise les agents à effectuer des analyses de qualité exhaustives sur les codebases en utilisant l''API Socket.dev et le SDK JavaScript, en identifiant les bogues critiques, les erreurs de logique et les problèmes de workflow via des agents spécialisés, tout en utilisant des dépendances comme socket-sdk-js et en générant des rapports prioritaires avec des tâches d''amélioration actionnables.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende Qualitätsprüfungen über Codebases hinweg durchzuführen, indem sie die Socket.dev-API und das JavaScript-SDK verwenden, um kritische Fehler, Logikfehler und Workflowprobleme durch spezielle Agenten zu identifizieren, während sie Abhängigkeiten wie socket-sdk-js nutzen und priorisierte Berichte mit ausführbaren Verbesserungsaufgaben generieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar varreduras de qualidade abrangentes em codebases usando a API Socket.dev e JavaScript SDK, identificando bugs críticos, erros de lógica e problemas de fluxo de trabalho por meio de agentes especializados, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza dependências como socket-sdk-js e gera relatórios priorizados com tarefas de melhoria executáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить комплексные проверки качества по кодовым базам с помощью API Socket.dev и JavaScript SDK, выявляя критические ошибки, логические ошибки и проблемы с рабочим процессом посредством специализированных агентов, а также использует зависимости, такие как socket-sdk-js, и генерирует отчеты с приоритизированными задачами по улучшению.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إجراء مسح شامل لجودة القواعد الكودية باستخدام API Socket.dev و JavaScript SDK ، وتحديد الأخطاء الحاسمة وأخطاء المنطق ومشاكل سير العمل من خلال وكلاء متخصصين ، وفي نفس الوقت استخدام التبعيات مثل socket-sdk-js وتوليد تقارير مفضلة مع مهام تحسين قابلة للتنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for JavaScript projects","Debugging socket-sdk-js integrations","Generating quality scan reports for repository maintenance"],"zh":["自动化JavaScript项目的代码审查","调试socket-sdk-js集成","为存储库维护生成质量扫描报告"],"ja":["JavaScriptプロジェクトのコードレビューの自動化","socket-sdk-js統合のデバッグ","リポジトリのメンテナンスのための品質スキャンレポートの生成"],"ko":["JavaScript 프로젝트의 코드 리뷰 자동화","socket-sdk-js 통합 디버깅","저장소 유지 보수를 위한 품질 스캔 보고서 생성"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para proyectos JavaScript","Depuración de integraciones de socket-sdk-js","Generación de informes de análisis de calidad para el mantenimiento de repositorios"],"fr":["Automatisation des revues de code pour les projets JavaScript","Débogage des intégrations de socket-sdk-js","Génération de rapports d''analyse de qualité pour la maintenance des référentiels"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für JavaScript-Projekte","Fehlerbehebung bei socket-sdk-js-Integrationen","Generierung von Qualitätsprüfberichten für die Wartung von Repositories"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para projetos JavaScript","Depurar integrações socket-sdk-js","Gerar relatórios de varredura de qualidade para manutenção de repositório"],"ru":["Автоматизация проверок кода для проектов JavaScript","Отладка интеграций socket-sdk-js","Генерация отчетов о проверке качества для обслуживания репозитория"],"ar":["تأتمة مراجعة الكود لمشاريع JavaScript","تصحيح أخطاء التكامل socket-sdk-js","إنشاء تقارير فحص الجودة لصيانة المستودع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Socket.dev API access","JavaScript SDK compatibility needed","Repository cleanup and dependency updates necessary"],"zh":["需要Socket.dev API访问","需要JavaScript SDK兼容性","需要存储库清理和依赖更新"],"ja":["Socket.dev APIへのアクセスが必要","JavaScript SDKの互換性が必要","リポジトリのクリーンアップと依存関係の更新が必要"],"ko":["Socket.dev API 액세스가 필요합니다.","JavaScript SDK 호환성이 필요합니다.","저장소 정리 및 종속성 업데이트가 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de Socket.dev","Se requiere compatibilidad con el SDK de JavaScript","Limpieza de repositorio y actualizaciones de dependencias necesarias"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API Socket.dev","Compatibilité du SDK JavaScript requise","Nettoyage du référentiel et mises à jour des dépendances nécessaires"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Socket.dev-API","JavaScript-SDK-Kompatibilität erforderlich","Repository-Reinigung und Abhängigkeits-Updates erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API Socket.dev","Compatibilidade com JavaScript SDK necessária","Limpeza de repositório e atualizações de dependência necessárias"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к API Socket.dev","Необходимо совместимость с JavaScript SDK","Необходимо очистка репозитория и обновления зависимостей"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى API Socket.dev","مطلوب توافق مع JavaScript SDK","مطلوب تنظيف المستودع و تحديث التبعيات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b2c15220d890b826c1ec850cb47775c008645ef0ea7c