egração com machine learning","Suporte a NLP para processamento de linguagem natural","Ferramenta de código aberto para desenvolvedores","Integração com hacktoberfest para contribuições comunitárias"],"ru":["Анализ вибраций для качественных исследований","Интеграция с машинным обучением","Поддержка NLP для обработки естественного языка","Инструмент с открытым исходным кодом для разработчиков","Интеграция с hacktoberfest для сообщественных вкладов"],"ar":["تحليل التفاعل للبحوث النوعية","التكامل مع التعلم الآلي","دعم NLP لمعالجة اللغة الطبيعية","أداة مفتوحة المصدر للمطورين","التكامل مع hacktoberfest للمساهمات المجتمعية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用CRISP-T AI智能工具","什么是定性研究","CRISP-T AI智能工具替代品","CRISP-T AI智能工具与竞争对手的比较","CRISP-T AI智能工具安装","CRISP-T AI智能工具设置指南","机器学习和自然语言处理","vibe分析","Hacktoberfest"],"ja":["CRISP-T AIエージェントの使用方法","定性的研究とは","CRISP-T AIエージェントの代替品","CRISP-T AIエージェントと競合製品の比較","CRISP-T AIエージェントのインストール","CRISP-T AIエージェントの設定ガイド","機械学習と自然言語処理","vibe分析","Hacktoberfest"],"ko":["CRISP-T AI 에이전트 사용 방법","정성 연구란","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 대체品","CRISP-T AI 에이전트와 경쟁 제품 비교","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 설치","CRISP-T AI 에이전트 설정 가이드","기계학습과 자연어 처리","바이브 분석","Hacktoberfest"],"es":["cómo usar CRISP-T","qué es la investigación cualitativa","alternativas a CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs herramientas de investigación cualitativa","instalación de CRISP-T","guía de configuración de CRISP-T","hacktoberfest proyectos","herramientas de IA para investigación cualitativa"],"fr":["comment utiliser CRISP-T","qu''est-ce que la recherche qualitative","alternatives à CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs outils de recherche qualitative","installation de CRISP-T","guide de configuration de CRISP-T","projets hacktoberfest","outils IA pour la recherche qualitative"],"de":["wie man CRISP-T verwendet","was ist qualitative Forschung","Alternativen zu CRISP-T","CRISP-T vs qualitative Forschungstools","Installation von CRISP-T","Konfigurationsanleitung für CRISP-T","Hacktoberfest-Projekte","KI-Tools für qualitative Forschung"],"pt":["como usar CRISP-T","o que é CRISP-T","ferramentas de IA para pesquisa qualitativa","CRISP-T vs outras ferramentas de IA","guia de instalação do CRISP-T","configuração do CRISP-T","CRISP-T para desenvolvedores","alternativas ao CRISP-T"],"ru":["как использовать CRISP-T","что такое CRISP-T","инструменты ИИ для качественных исследований","CRISP-T vs другие инструменты ИИ","руководство по установке CRISP-T","настройка CRISP-T","CRISP-T для разработчиков","альтернативы CRISP-T"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام CRISP-T","ما هو CRISP-T","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للبحوث النوعية","CRISP-T مقابل أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي الأخرى","دليل تثبيت CRISP-T","إعداد CRISP-T","CRISP-T للمطورين","بديلات CRISP-T"]}},"owner":"dermatologist","repo":"crisp-t","repoPath":"dermatologist/crisp-t","stars":8,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T22:06:45Z","topics":["hacktoberfest","machine-learning","nlp","qualitative-research"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"crisp-mcp","description":"Use the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full qualitative analysis workflow linking textual narratives and numeric data.","bodyPreview":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analys","body":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analysis, triangulation, and export**\n- The model can **discover tools at runtime** and adapt to the actual tool list\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to:\n\n- Explore and code qualitative data (e.g., interviews, narratives, open‑ended survey responses)\n- Triangulate qualitative codes with quantitative variables\n- Produce **transparent, reproducible outputs** (memos, codebooks, matrices, summaries)\n\n---\n\n## Intended users and scenarios\n\n- **Qualitative / mixed‑methods researchers** working with text + numeric data\n\nTypical scenarios:\n\n- Coding COVID‑era patient narratives and linking them to open‑source epidemiological data\n- Triangulating interview themes with survey scores or EHR‑derived indicators\n- Building theory from mixed text–numeric corpora using CRISP‑T stages\n\n---\n\n## MCP server and tools\n\n### Server\n\n- **Server name (example):** `crisp-t`\n- **Protocol:** Model Context Protocol (MCP) via stdio (e.g., `crisp-mcp`)\n\n> **Important:**\n> Use ./workspace as the working directory for all artifacts, if not explicitly specified. Create it if it does not exist.\n> Always **discover** the available tools from the CRISP‑T MCP server first, then map them to the workflow below.\n> Tool names in this file are **illustrative**; prefer the *actual* tool names and schemas exposed by the server.\n\n## Recommended steps\n* Import data into CRISP-T corpus and dataframe.\n* Perform linking between text and numeric data using various methods (id based, keyword based, time based, embedding based).\n* Explore text data using various methods (e.g., topic modeling, keyword extraction, sentiment analysis, visualizations).\n* Explore numeric data using various methods (e.g., summary statistics, classification, clustering, regression, association, visualizations, TDA, etc.).\n* Perform cross modal analysis using linked text and numeric data (e.g., text features as predictors for numeric outcomes, numeric features as predictors for text outcomes, etc.).\n* Add manual connections between text documents and numeric rows if needed to support theory driven analysis.\n* Derive insights from the analysis and document them.\n\n### Expected tool capabilities (illustrative)\n\nWhen you discover tools from the `crisp-t` MCP server, look for tools that correspond to the following capabilities:\n\n1. **Project and configuration**\n   - **List / load projects** (e.g., `list_projects`, `load_project`)\n   - **List / configure data sources** (text + numeric)\n\n2. **Textual data operations**\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., documents, transcripts, narrative files)\n   - **Fetch text segments** (e.g., by document, case, or segment ID)\n   - **Apply or update codes** to segments\n   - **List codes / categories / codebook**\n\n3. **Numeric / structured data operations**\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., CSVs, tables)\n   - **Fetch rows / variables** for a given case or group\n   - **Run basic summaries or models** (e.g., descriptive stats, correlations)\n\n4. **Triangulation / integration**\n   - **Link coded text segments to numeric data** by case ID or key\n   - **Generate triangulation matrices** (codes × variables, cases × themes, etc.)\n   - **Compute simple indicators** (e.g., frequency, co‑occurrence, association)\n\n5. **Memoing and export**\n   - **Create / update analytic memos**\n   - **Export codebooks, matrices, and summaries** (e.g., CSV, JSON, Markdown)\n   - **Save session context or analysis snapshots**\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Inspect tool descriptions and schemas**\n- **Prefer higher‑level CRISP‑T tools** (e.g., “triangulate”, “inspect”, “sense‑make”) over low‑level primitives when available\n- **Avoid guessing tool parameters**—use the schema and ask the user when needed\n\n---\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe user may provide some or all of the following. If missing, ask concise clarification questions.\n\n- **Research question / focus**\n  - `research_question`: short description of what they want to understand or explain\n- **Project / dataset selection**\n  - `project_name` or `project_id`\n  - `text_source_pattern` (e.g., “patient_narratives”, “interviews_*”)\n  - `numeric_dataset_name` (e.g., “covid_metrics.csv”, “survey_scores”)\n- **Methodological preferences**\n  - `coding_style`: open coding, focused coding, or using an existing codebook\n  - `triangulation_focus`: e.g., “compare themes by age group”, “link narratives to hospitalization status”\n- **Output preferences**\n  - `output_format`: Markdown, CSV, JSON, or mixed\n  - `audience`: “methods‑savvy colleague”, “student”, “grant reviewer”, etc.\n\nIf the user is vague, default to:\n\n- Open coding → focused coding\n- Simple triangulation (themes × one or two key numeric variables)\n- Markdown summaries plus CSV exports where supported\n\n---\n\n## Outputs\n\nThis skill should aim to produce:\n\n1. **Analytic memo**\n   - Research question and context\n   - Data sources used (text + numeric)\n   - Coding approach and key categories\n   - Triangulation findings (convergences, divergences, surprises)\n   - Limitations and next steps\n\n2. **Structured artifacts** (when tools support them)\n   - Codebook (codes, definitions, examples)\n   - Triangulation matrix (e.g., codes × variables)\n   - Exported files (CSV/JSON/Markdown) referenced in the memo\n\n3. **Reproducible trace**\n   - Clear description of which MCP tools were called\n   - Parameters used (e.g., filters, variables, thresholds)\n   - Any important analytic decisions made during the session\n\n---\n\n## High‑level workflow\n\nYou should follow this workflow, adapting to the actual CRISP‑T tools you discover.\n\n### 1. Clarify research focus and context\n\n1. **Summarize the user’s goal** in 2–3 sentences.\n2. If unclear, ask **one or two** focused questions:\n   - **Example:** “Which is more important right now: exploring themes, or linking themes to numeric outcomes?”\n3. Record the clarified research question in the analytic memo.\n\n### 2. Discover CRISP‑T MCP tools and project context\n\n1. **List available tools** from the `crisp-t` MCP server.\n2. Identify tools that correspond to:\n   - Project management\n   - Text operations\n   - Numeric operations\n   - Triangulation\n   - Memoing / export\n3. If available, **list projects** and either:\n   - Load the project specified by the user, or\n   - Present a short list and ask the user to choose.\n\nDocument in the memo:\n\n- Which project was loaded\n- Which tools will be used and for what purpose\n\n### 3. Inspect data sources (text + numeric)\n\n1. Use project / data tools to:\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., narrative collections, interview sets)\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., survey tables, EHR‑derived tables)\n2. For each candidate source:\n   - Fetch a **small sample** (e.g., a few narratives, a few rows of numeric data)\n   - Briefly describe:\n     - What the data represent\n     - How they relate to the research question\n3. Confirm with the user which sources to prioritize.\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- Selected text sources and why\n- Selected numeric datasets and why\n\n### 4. Initial coding of qualitative data (open / exploratory)\n\n1. Select a **manageable subset** of text (e.g., 10–20 narratives or segments).\n2. Apply **open coding** using the CRISP‑T coding tools:\n   - Generate **short, grounded codes** that stay close to the data\n   - Avoid premature theory; focus on what participants are saying/doing/experiencing\n3. Use MCP tools to:\n   - Save codes to the project\n   - Attach codes to segments\n   - Retrieve and refine the emerging code list\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe the coding approach (e.g., open coding, line‑by‑line, incident‑focused)\n- Provide **examples**: quote → code → brief interpretation\n\n### 5. Focused coding and category development\n\n1. Review the emerging code list using CRISP‑T tools (e.g., list codes, code frequencies).\n2. Group related codes into **higher‑level categories** or themes:\n   - Merge overlapping codes\n   - Distinguish closely related but conceptually different codes\n3. If the server supports it, create or update:\n   - A **codebook** (code name, definition, inclusion/exclusion criteria, example quotes)\n   - **Category structures** (e.g., parent/child relationships)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe key categories and how they were derived\n- Note any tensions, ambiguities, or alternative interpretations\n\n### 6. Computational triangulation with numeric data\n\nUsing CRISP‑T tools that link text and numeric data:\n\n1. **Identify the linkage key** (e.g., participant ID, case ID, encounter ID).\n2. For each case or group:\n   - Retrieve **coded qualitative data** (codes, categories, or themes)\n   - Retrieve **numeric variables** (e.g., age, scores, outcomes, counts)\n3. Construct **triangulation views**, such as:\n   - Code frequencies by group (e.g., theme prevalence by age band or outcome)\n   - Associations between codes and numeric indicators (e.g., high vs. low scores)\n   - Patterns of convergence (where qualitative and quantitative tell a similar story)\n   - Patterns of divergence (where they conflict or complicate each other)\n\nWhen tools support it, generate:\n\n- **Triangulation matrices** (e.g., codes × variables, cases × themes)\n- **Summary statistics** (e.g., counts, proportions, simple associations)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe **how** triangulation was done (data sources, linkage, variables)\n- Highlight **convergences, divergences, and surprises**\n- Emphasize that triangulation is about **enriching and challenging** interpretations, not “proving” them\n\n### 7. Synthesis and theory‑building\n\n1. Integrate insights from:\n   - Qualitative categories and themes\n   - Numeric patterns and contrasts\n   - Triangulation matrices and summaries\n2. Propose **tentative theoretical statements** or propositions:\n   - “In this context, participants who X tend to Y, especially when Z…”\n3. Explicitly note:\n   - Alternative explanations\n   - Data limitations\n   - What additional data or analysis would strengthen the claims\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- A **coherent narrative** that links data, codes, categories, and numeric patterns\n- Clear statements about **what the data support** and **what remains uncertain**\n\n### 8. Export and documentation\n\n1. Use CRISP‑T export tools to save:\n   - Codebook(s)\n   - Triangulation matrices\n   - Any generated summaries or tables\n2. If supported, export:\n   - The analytic memo as Markdown or another requested format\n   - A machine‑readable representation of the analysis (e.g., JSON snapshot)\n\nProvide the user with:\n\n- A **human‑readable summary** (memo)\n- A **list of exported artifacts** and where they are stored (paths, IDs, or URLs)\n\n---\n\n## Model behavior and style guidelines\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Be methodologically explicit**\n  - Name what you are doing (open coding, focused coding, triangulation, memoing)\n  - Briefly justify key analytic decisions\n- **Stay grounded in the data**\n  - Use short quotes and concrete examples\n  - Avoid over‑generalizing beyond what the data support\n- **Respect the user’s context**\n  - If they are teaching, highlight steps and rationale for students\n  - If they are writing a paper or grant, emphasize clarity and traceability\n- **Limit questions**\n  - Ask at most **one or two** focused questions at a time\n  - Default to reasonable assumptions when the user is not specific\n\n---\n\n## Limitations and cautions\n\n- Triangulation results should be treated as **aids to interpretation**, not definitive proof.\n- Always encourage the user to:\n  - Review codes and categories\n  - Challenge interpretations\n  - Consider ethical and contextual factors not visible in the data\n\n---\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T13:12:05.091Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Qualitative Research Agents needing AI-assisted content analysis with vibe analytics and computational triangulation.","zh":"非常适合需要使用人工智能辅助内容分析、氛围分析和计算三角测量的定性研究代理。","ja":"AIアシストのコンテンツ分析、バイブ分析、計算三角測量を必要とする定性研究エージェントに最適です。","ko":"인공 지능으로辅助된 内容 분석, 분위기 분석 및 계산 삼각 측량이 필요한 질적 연구 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de investigación cualitativa que necesitan análisis de contenido asistido por IA con análisis de vibraciones y triangulación computacional.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de recherche qualitative ayant besoin d''une analyse de contenu assistée par l''IA avec des analyses de vibrations et une triangulation computationnelle.","de":"Perfekt für qualitative Forschungsagenten, die eine AI-gestützte Inhaltsanalyse mit Vibroanalytik und computergestützter Triangulation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Pesquisa Qualitativa que necessitam de análise de conteúdo assistida por IA com análise de vibrações e triangulação computacional.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов качественных исследований, которым требуется анализ контента с помощью ИИ с помощью анализа настроений и вычислительной триангуляции.","ar":"مثالي لعميل البحث النوعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل المحتوى المدعوم بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع تحليل الاهتزازات والثلاثية الحاسوبية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive qualitative analysis workflows using the CRISP-T MCP server, linking textual narratives and numeric data through grounded theory-inspired coding and exposing tools for corpus management, text coding, and numeric analysis via protocols like MCP.","zh":"赋予代理人使用CRISP-T MCP服务器执行全面的定性分析工作流的能力，通过接地理論启发的编码将文本叙述和数值数据链接起来，并通过诸如MCP的协议暴露语料库管理、文本编码和数值分析工具。","ja":"CRISP-T MCPサーバーを使用して、総合的な定性分析ワークフローを実行するエージェントを可能にし、地理理論に基づくコーディングによってテキストの物語と数値データをリンクし、MCPなどのプロトコルを介してコーパス管理、テキストコーディング、数値分析ツールを公開します。","ko":"에이전트가 CRISP-T MCP 서버를 사용하여 포괄적인 질적 분석 워크플로를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 근거 이론에启发한 코딩을 통해 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터를 연결하고, MCP와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 코퍼스 관리, 텍스트 코딩 및 수치 분석 도구를 노출합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar flujos de trabajo de análisis cualitativo integral utilizando el servidor CRISP-T MCP, vinculando narrativas textuales y datos numéricos a través de codificación inspirada en la teoría fundamentada y exponiendo herramientas para la gestión de corpus, codificación de texto y análisis numérico a través de protocolos como MCP.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des flux de travail d''analyse qualitative complets en utilisant le serveur CRISP-T MCP, en reliant des récits textuels et des données numériques à travers un codage inspiré de la théorie ancrée et en exposant des outils pour la gestion de corpus, le codage de texte et l''analyse numérique via des protocoles tels que MCP.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende qualitative Analyse-Workflows mit dem CRISP-T MCP-Server durchzuführen, indem textuelle Erzählungen und numerische Daten durch kodierungsinspirierte Theorie verknüpft und Werkzeuge für die Korpusverwaltung, Textcodierung und numerische Analyse über Protokolle wie MCP bereitgestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar fluxos de trabalho de análise qualitativa abrangente usando o servidor CRISP-T MCP, vinculando narrativas textuais e dados numéricos por meio de codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada e expondo ferramentas para gerenciamento de corpus, codificação de texto e análise numérica por meio de protocolos como o MCP.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять комплексные потоки работ качественного анализа с помощью сервера CRISP-T MCP, связывая текстовые нарративы и числовые данные посредством кодирования, вдохновленного основанной теорией, и предоставляя инструменты для управления корпусом, кодирования текста и числового анализа через протоколы, такие как MCP.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على أداء تدفقات عمل تحليل نوعي شاملة باستخدام خادم CRISP-T MCP، ويربط السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية من خلال الترميز الذي يلهم نظرية أساسية وتوفر أدوات لإدارة المحتوى وترميز النص والتحليل الرقمي من خلال بروتوكولات مثل MCP."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating qualitative research workflows with computational triangulation","Generating insights from textual narratives and numeric data using grounded theory-inspired coding","Managing corpora and performing text coding on the CRISP-T MCP server"],"zh":["使用计算三角测量自动化定性研究工作流程","使用接地理論启发的编码从文本叙述和数值数据中生成见解","在CRISP-T MCP服务器上管理语料库并执行文本编码"],"ja":["計算三角測量を使用して定性研究ワークフローを自動化する","地理理論に基づくコーディングを使用してテキストの物語と数値データからインサイトを生成する","CRISP-T MCPサーバー上でコーパスを管理し、テキストコーディングを実行する"],"ko":["계산 삼각 측량을 사용하여 질적 연구 워크플로를 자동화하는 것","근거 이론에启发한 코딩을 사용하여 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터에서 인사이트를 생성하는 것","CRISP-T MCP 서버에서 코퍼스를 관리하고 텍스트 코딩을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de investigación cualitativa con triangulación computacional","Generación de conocimientos a partir de narrativas textuales y datos numéricos utilizando codificación inspirada en la teoría fundamentada","Gestión de corpus y realización de codificación de texto en el servidor CRISP-T MCP"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de recherche qualitative avec triangulation computationnelle","Génération d''informations à partir de récits textuels et de données numériques en utilisant un codage inspiré de la théorie ancrée","Gestion de corpus et réalisation de codage de texte sur le serveur CRISP-T MCP"],"de":["Automatisierung qualitativer Forschungs-Workflows mit computergestützter Triangulation","Erzeugung von Erkenntnissen aus textuellen Erzählungen und numerischen Daten unter Verwendung von kodierungsinspirierter Theorie","Verwaltung von Korpora und Durchführung von Textcodierung auf dem CRISP-T MCP-Server"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de pesquisa qualitativa com triangulação computacional","Gerar insights a partir de narrativas textuais e dados numéricos usando codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada","Gerenciar corpora e realizar codificação de texto no servidor CRISP-T MCP"],"ru":["Автоматизировать потоки работ качественных исследований с помощью вычислительной триангуляции","Генерировать идеи из текстовых нарративов и числовых данных с помощью кодирования, вдохновленного основанной теорией","Управлять корпусом и выполнять кодирование текста на сервере CRISP-T MCP"],"ar":["أتمتة تدفقات عمل البحث النوعي مع ثلاثية الحاسوبية","توليد رؤى من السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية باستخدام الترميز الذي يلهم نظرية أساسية","إدارة المحتوى وتنفيذ ترميز النص على خادم CRISP-T MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires CRISP-T MCP server availability","Falls back to crisp-cli skill if CRISP-T MCP server is not found"],"zh":["需要CRISP-T MCP服务器可用性","如果CRISP-T MCP服务器未找到，则回退到crisp-cli技能"],"ja":["CRISP-T MCPサーバーの可用性が必要","CRISP-T MCPサーバーが見つからない場合、crisp-cliスキルにフォールバック"],"ko":["CRISP-T MCP 서버의 가용성이 필요함","CRISP-T MCP 서버가 발견되지 않을 경우 crisp-cli 스킬로 돌아감"],"es":["Requiere la disponibilidad del servidor CRISP-T MCP","Vuelve a la habilidad crisp-cli si el servidor CRISP-T MCP no se encuentra"],"fr":["Nécessite la disponibilité du serveur CRISP-T MCP","Reviens à la compétence crisp-cli si le serveur CRISP-T MCP n''est pas trouvé"],"de":["Benötigt die Verfügbarkeit des CRISP-T MCP-Servers","Fällt auf die crisp-cli-Fähigkeit zurück, wenn der CRISP-T MCP-Server nicht gefunden wird"],"pt":["Exige disponibilidade do servidor CRISP-T MCP","Volta para a habilidade crisp-cli se o servidor CRISP-T MCP não for encontrado"],"ru":["Требует доступности сервера CRISP-T MCP","Переходит на способность crisp-cli, если сервер CRISP-T MCP не найден"],"ar":["يتطلب توافر خادم CRISP-T MCP","يتخلف إلى مهارة crisp-cli إذا لم يكن خادم CRISP-T MCP موجودًا"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"fcb7d601db4a386ea6e1520042c43c9d27111b990bdc518bbf37564c4e3c4ba2","qualityScore":45}');
