ur fluide","Design inspiré de la nature pour une atmosphère relaxante","Outils de communauté pour se connecter avec d''autres blogueurs","Intégration avec Cloudflare pour un chargement rapide et sécurisé","Compatibilité avec les appareils mobiles pour une expérience partout"],"de":["SvelteKit-Technologie für eine flüssige Benutzererfahrung","Naturinspiriertes Design für eine entspannte Atmosphäre","Community-Tools für die Verbindung mit anderen Bloggern","Integration mit Cloudflare für ein schnelles und sicheres Laden","Kompatibilität mit mobilen Geräten für eine Erfahrung überall"],"pt":["Tecnologia Sveltekit","Integração com Cloudflare","Ferramentas de comunidade","Tema inspirado na natureza","Suporte à comunidade indie-web","Recursos para bloggers queer e solarpunk"],"ru":["Технология Sveltekit","Интеграция с Cloudflare","Инструменты для сообщества","Тема, вдохновленная природой","Поддержка сообщества indie-web","Возможности для блогеров queer и solarpunk"],"ar":["تكنولوجيا Sveltekit","التكامل مع Cloudflare","أدوات المجتمع","موضوع مستوحى من الطبيعة","دعم المجتمع indie-web","ميزات للمدونين المثليين وسولار بانك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用elephant-build","什么是独立网络","elephant-build替代品","elephant-build与Ghost比较","elephant-build安装指南","SvelteKit开发教程","Cloudflare内容分发网络","Solarpunk社区建设"],"ja":["elephant-buildの使い方","インディーウェブとは","elephant-buildの代替","elephant-buildとGhostの比較","elephant-buildのインストールガイド","SvelteKit開発チュートリアル","CloudflareのCDN","ソーラーパンクコミュニティの構築"],"ko":["elephant-build 사용법","독립적인 웹이란","elephant-build 대체품","elephant-build와 Ghost 비교","elephant-build 설치 가이드","SvelteKit 개발 튜토리얼","Cloudflare의 CDN","솔라펑크 커뮤니티 구축"],"es":["herramientas de blogging","tecnología SvelteKit","diseño inspirado en la naturaleza","herramientas de comunidad","Cloudflare","cómo usar elephant-build","alternativas a elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"fr":["outils de blogging","technologie SvelteKit","design inspiré de la nature","outils de communauté","Cloudflare","comment utiliser elephant-build","alternatives à elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"de":["Blogging-Tools","SvelteKit-Technologie","naturinspiriertes Design","Community-Tools","Cloudflare","wie man elephant-build verwendet","Alternativen zu elephant-build","elephant-build vs WordPress"],"pt":["como usar elephant-build","o que é elephant-build","elephant-build vs wordpress","elephant-build alternative","instalar elephant-build","guia de configuração do elephant-build","desenvolvedores de elephant-build","ferramentas de IA para blogging","tecnologias de comunidade indie-web"],"ru":["как использовать elephant-build","что такое elephant-build","elephant-build vs wordpress","альтернатива elephant-build","установить elephant-build","руководство по настройке elephant-build","разработчики elephant-build","инструменты ИИ для блогинга","технологии для сообщества indie-web"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة elephant-build","ما هي أداة elephant-build","أداة elephant-build مقابل ووردبريس","بديل أداة elephant-build","تثبيت أداة elephant-build","دليل إعداد أداة elephant-build","مطورو أداة elephant-build","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمدونات","تكنولوجيا المجتمع indie-web"]}},"owner":"AutumnsGrove","repo":"Lattice","repoPath":"AutumnsGrove/Lattice","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T00:00:53Z","topics":["blogging","cloudflare","indie-web","nature-themed","queer","solarpunk","sveltekit"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"elephant-build","description":"Build multi-file features with unstoppable momentum. Trumpet the vision, gather materials, construct with strength, test thoroughly, and celebrate completion. Use when implementing features that span multiple files or systems.","bodyPreview":"# Elephant Build 🐘\n\nThe elephant doesn''t hesitate. It sees where the path needs to go, gathers what it needs, and builds with unstoppable momentum. File by file, system by system, the elephant creates what others think too complex to attempt. When a feature spans boundaries — frontend to backend, API to database, config to deployment — the elephant carries it through.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User asks to \"implement this feature\" or \"build this system\"\n- User says \"create\" something that needs m","body":"# Elephant Build 🐘\n\nThe elephant doesn''t hesitate. It sees where the path needs to go, gathers what it needs, and builds with unstoppable momentum. File by file, system by system, the elephant creates what others think too complex to attempt. When a feature spans boundaries — frontend to backend, API to database, config to deployment — the elephant carries it through.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User asks to \"implement this feature\" or \"build this system\"\n- User says \"create\" something that needs multiple files\n- User calls `/elephant-build` or mentions elephant/building\n- Features spanning frontend + backend + database\n- New API endpoints with client integration\n- Database migrations with code changes\n- Complex UI flows with state management\n- Anything requiring coordinated changes across modules\n\n**Pair with:** `bloodhound-scout` for exploration first, `beaver-build` for testing after\n\n---\n\n## The Build\n\n```\nTRUMPET → GATHER → BUILD → TEST → CELEBRATE\n    ↓        ↓        ↲        ↓         ↓\nDeclare  Collect   Construct Validate   Complete\nVision   Materials  Power    Strength   Triumph\n```\n\n### Phase 1: TRUMPET\n\n_The elephant lifts its trunk and sounds the beginning..._\n\nDeclare what we''re building with full scope clarity.\n\n- Write one sentence: what does this feature DO for users?\n- Define scope boundaries — what''s IN and explicitly what''s OUT\n- Create the file inventory: new files, modified files, config changes\n- Establish build sequence: schema → services → API → UI → integration → tests\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/file-patterns.md` for SvelteKit file patterns, component structure, and API route conventions\n\n**Output:** Clear vision, scope boundaries, file inventory, and build sequence\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: GATHER\n\n_The elephant collects stones and branches, preparing the foundation..._\n\nCollect everything needed before building begins.\n\n- Check dependencies — verify required packages exist, install what''s missing\n- Research existing patterns with `gf --agent usage \"ServiceName\"` and `gf --agent func \"functionName\"`\n- Examine similar implementations to understand conventions before diverging\n- Set up environment variables in `.env.local` and `.env.example`\n\n**Output:** All materials gathered, dependencies ready, patterns understood\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: BUILD\n\n_The elephant places each stone with precision, building what will last..._\n\nConstruct the feature file by file, in order.\n\n- Database/Foundation first (schema, types, constants)\n- Backend Services second (business logic, data access)\n- API Layer third (endpoints, validation, error handling)\n- Frontend Components fourth (UI, state management)\n- Integration last (wiring it all together)\n- One file at a time — finish it before moving on\n- Follow existing patterns — match the codebase style\n- Use Signpost error codes on every error path\n- Validate all inputs; add TypeScript types throughout\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/build-checklist.md` for the multi-file build checklist, integration wiring steps, and database schema patterns\n\n**Reference:** Load `references/signpost-errors.md` for Signpost error codes, which helper to use where, and toast feedback patterns\n\n**Output:** Complete implementation across all required files\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: TEST\n\n_The elephant tests each stone, ensuring the structure holds..._\n\n**MANDATORY: Verify the build before committing. The elephant does not ship broken structures.**\n\n```bash\npnpm install\ngw ci --affected --fail-fast --diagnose\n```\n\nIf verification fails: read the diagnostics, fix the errors, re-run verification. Repeat until the structure holds.\n\nOnce CI passes, verify manually:\n- Happy path works end-to-end\n- Error states handled gracefully\n- Loading states work\n- Mobile layout correct\n- Keyboard navigation and accessibility pass\n\n**Output:** All tests passing, manual verification complete, edge cases handled\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: CELEBRATE\n\n_The elephant raises its trunk in triumph, the build complete..._\n\nShip and document.\n\n```bash\ngw git ship --write -a -m \"feat(component): brief description of feature\"\n```\n\nWrite the completion summary: files created, files modified, config changes, tests added, verification status.\n\n**Output:** Feature complete, tested, documented, and ready for production\n\n---\n\n## Reference Routing Table\n\n| Phase | Reference | Load When |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| TRUMPET | `references/file-patterns.md` | Planning new SvelteKit files |\n| BUILD | `references/build-checklist.md` | Tracking multi-file construction |\n| BUILD | `references/signpost-errors.md` | Implementing error handling |\n\n---\n\n## Elephant Rules\n\n### Momentum\n\nKeep moving forward. Don''t get stuck on one file for hours. If blocked, make a TODO and move on. The elephant doesn''t stop.\n\n### Completeness\n\nBuild the whole feature. Half-built features don''t help users. If the scope is too big, scope down — but finish what you start.\n\n### Quality\n\nBuild it right the first time. Tests, error handling, types — these aren''t extras, they''re part of the build.\n\n### Communication\n\nUse building metaphors:\n\n- \"Sounding the trumpet...\" (declaring the vision)\n- \"Gathering materials...\" (preparation)\n- \"Placing each stone...\" (construction)\n- \"Testing the structure...\" (validation)\n- \"Build complete!\" (celebration)\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n**The elephant does NOT:**\n\n- Start building without understanding the scope\n- Skip tests because \"we''ll add them later\"\n- Leave TODO comments instead of finishing\n- Break existing functionality\n- Ignore error cases for the happy path\n- Copy-paste without understanding\n\n---\n\n## Example Build\n\n**User:** \"Add a comments system to blog posts\"\n\n**Elephant flow:**\n\n1. 🐘 **TRUMPET** — \"Users can leave threaded comments on blog posts. Scope: basic CRUD, threaded replies, moderation. Out: real-time updates, reactions.\"\n\n2. 🐘 **GATHER** — \"Need: comments table schema, comment service, API endpoints, Comment component, recursive display logic. Check: existing auth patterns, how posts work.\"\n\n3. 🐘 **BUILD** — \"Schema → Service (CRUD + threading) → API endpoints → CommentList/CommentForm components → Wire into post page → Add moderation UI\"\n\n4. 🐘 **TEST** — \"Unit tests for service, integration tests for API, component tests for UI, manual test of threading depth limit\"\n\n5. 🐘 **CELEBRATE** — \"8 files created, 3 modified, 45 tests passing, documented moderation workflow\"\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**Before Building:** `bloodhound-scout` — Explore existing patterns; `eagle-architect` — For complex system design; `swan-design` — If detailed specs needed\n\n**During Building:** `chameleon-adapt` — For UI polish; `beaver-build` — For testing strategy\n\n**After Building:** `raccoon-audit` — Security review; `fox-optimize` — If performance issues found; `deer-sense` — Accessibility audit\n\n---\n\n_What seems impossible alone becomes inevitable with the elephant''s momentum._ 🐘\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:40:45.018Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Agents needing comprehensive system development capabilities from frontend to backend, including API and database integration.","zh":"非常适合需要从前端到后端的全面系统开发能力的全栈代理，包括API和数据库集成。","ja":"フルスタックエージェントがフロントエンドからバックエンドまで、APIやデータベース統合を含む包括的なシステム開発機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"전면부터 후면까지 API 및 데이터베이스 통합을 포함한 포괄적인 시스템 개발 기능이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Full-Stack que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo de sistemas integrales desde el frontend hasta el backend, incluyendo la integración de API y base de datos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents Full-Stack ayant besoin de capacités de développement de systèmes complètes du frontend au backend, y compris l''intégration d''API et de base de données.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die umfassende Systementwicklungsfähigkeiten vom Frontend bis zum Backend benötigen, einschließlich API- und Datenbankintegration.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full-Stack que necessitam de capacidades de desenvolvimento de sistema abrangentes, desde o frontend até o backend, incluindo integração de API e banco de dados.","ru":"Идеально для полнофункциональных агентов, которым необходимы комплексные возможности разработки системы от frontend до backend, включая интеграцию API и базы данных.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الكاملون الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات تطوير نظام شاملة من الجانب الأمامي إلى الجانب الخلفي، بما في ذلك دمج API وقاعدة البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create complex systems file by file, spanning boundaries from frontend to backend, API to database, and config to deployment, using unstoppable momentum to carry features through to completion, leveraging system integration and deployment protocols.","zh":"赋予代理创建复杂系统的能力，从文件到文件，跨越从前端到后端、API到数据库、配置到部署的边界，利用不可阻挡的动力将功能带到完成，利用系统集成和部署协议。","ja":"エージェントに、ファイルからファイルまで、フロントエンドからバックエンド、APIからデータベース、コンフィグからデプロイまでの境界を越えて複雑なシステムを作成する力を与え、停止不能の勢いを利用して機能を完了まで持ち込み、システム統合とデプロイプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 파일부터 파일까지, 전면부터 후면까지, API부터 데이터베이스까지, 구성부터 배포까지의 경계를越えて 복잡한 시스템을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 중단할 수 없는 추세를 활용하여 기능을 완성까지 가져가고, 시스템 통합 및 배포 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear sistemas complejos archivo por archivo, que abarcan fronteras desde el frontend hasta el backend, API hasta base de datos y configuración hasta implementación, utilizando un impulso imparable para llevar las características hasta su finalización, aprovechando los protocolos de integración y implementación del sistema.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des systèmes complexes fichier par fichier, qui s''étendent sur les frontières du frontend au backend, de l''API à la base de données et de la configuration à la mise en production, en utilisant une impulsion inarrêtable pour mener les fonctionnalités à leur achèvement, en exploitant les protocoles d''intégration et de déploiement du système.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, komplexe Systeme Datei für Datei zu erstellen, die Grenzen vom Frontend bis zum Backend, von API bis Datenbank und von Konfiguration bis Deployment überschreiten, unter Nutzung eines unstopzbaren Impulses, um Funktionen bis zur Fertigstellung zu tragen, unter Ausnutzung der Systemintegrations- und Deploymentsprotokolle.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar sistemas complexos arquivo por arquivo, abrangendo limites do frontend ao backend, API ao banco de dados e configuração à implantação, usando o ímpeto ininterrupto para levar os recursos até a conclusão, aproveitando protocolos de integração e implantação do sistema.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать сложные системы файл за файлом, охватывая границы от frontend до backend, API до базы данных и конфигурации до развертывания, используя непрерывный импульс для продвижения функций до завершения, используя протоколы интеграции и развертывания системы.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء أنظمة معقدة ملفًا بملف، متجاوزين الحدود من الجانب الأمامي إلى الجانب الخلفي، و API إلى قاعدة البيانات، وتكوين إلى نشر، باستخدام الزخم الذي لا يتوقف لتقديم الميزات إلى الانتهاء، واستخدام بروتوكولات التكامل والنشر للنظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Building comprehensive systems that integrate frontend and backend functionalities","Implementing features that span multiple system boundaries, including API and database interactions","Creating and deploying complex configurations across different environments"],"zh":["构建集成前端和后端功能的综合系统","实现跨多个系统边界的功能，包括API和数据库交互","在不同环境中创建和部署复杂配置"],"ja":["フロントエンドとバックエンドの機能を統合した包括的なシステムを構築する","複数のシステム境界を越えた機能を実装する、APIやデータベースの相互作用を含む","さまざまな環境で複雑な構成を作成してデプロイする"],"ko":["전면과 후면 기능을 통합한 포괄적인 시스템을 구축하는 것","다수의 시스템 경계를越えた 기능을 구현하는 것, API 및 데이터베이스 상호 작용을 포함","다른 환경에서 복잡한 구성を作成하여 배포하는 것"],"es":["Construir sistemas integrales que integren funcionalidades de frontend y backend","Implementar características que abarcan múltiples fronteras de sistema, incluyendo interacciones de API y base de datos","Crear e implementar configuraciones complejas en diferentes entornos"],"fr":["Construire des systèmes complets qui intègrent des fonctionnalités de frontend et de backend","Mettre en œuvre des fonctionnalités qui s''étendent sur plusieurs frontières de système, y compris les interactions d''API et de base de données","Créer et déployer des configurations complexes dans différents environnements"],"de":["Umfassende Systeme aufbauen, die Frontend- und Backend-Funktionalitäten integrieren","Funktionen implementieren, die mehrere Systemgrenzen überschreiten, einschließlich API- und Datenbankinteraktionen","Komplexe Konfigurationen in verschiedenen Umgebungen erstellen und bereitstellen"],"pt":["Construir sistemas abrangentes que integrem funcionalidades de frontend e backend","Implementar recursos que abranjam múltiplas fronteiras do sistema, incluindo interações de API e banco de dados","Criar e implantar configurações complexas em diferentes ambientes"],"ru":["Построение комплексных систем, которые интегрируют функциональности frontend и backend","Реализация функций, охватывающих несколько границ системы, включая взаимодействия API и базы данных","Создание и развертывание сложных конфигураций в различных средах"],"ar":["بناء أنظمة شاملة تدمج وظائف الجانب الأمامي والجانب الخلفي","تنفيذ ميزات تتقاطع مع حدود متعددة للنظام، بما في ذلك التفاعلات مع API وقاعدة البيانات","إنشاء ونشر تكوينات معقدة في بيئات مختلفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear user requests to implement or build specific features or systems","May need additional tools or libraries for specific frontend, backend, API, or database functionalities"],"zh":["需要明确的用户请求来实现或构建特定的功能或系统","可能需要额外的工具或库来实现特定的前端、后端、API或数据库功能"],"ja":["特定の機能やシステムを実装または構築するために明確なユーザー要求が必要","特定のフロントエンド、バックエンド、APIまたはデータベースの機能を実現するために追加のツールまたはライブラリが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["특정 기능이나 시스템을 구현 또는 구축하기 위해 명확한 사용자 요청이 필요함","특정 전면, 후면, API 또는 데이터베이스 기능을 구현하기 위해 추가 도구 또는 라이브러리가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere solicitudes de usuario claras para implementar o construir características o sistemas específicos","Puede necesitar herramientas o bibliotecas adicionales para funcionalidades de frontend, backend, API o base de datos específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite des demandes d''utilisateur claires pour mettre en œuvre ou construire des fonctionnalités ou des systèmes spécifiques","Peut nécessiter des outils ou des bibliothèques supplémentaires pour des fonctionnalités de frontend, de backend, d''API ou de base de données spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt klare Benutzeranfragen, um bestimmte Funktionen oder Systeme zu implementieren oder zu erstellen","Benötigt möglicherweise zusätzliche Tools oder Bibliotheken für bestimmte Frontend-, Backend-, API- oder Datenbankfunktionalitäten"],"pt":["Exige solicitações de usuário claras para implementar ou construir recursos ou sistemas específicos","Pode precisar de ferramentas ou bibliotecas adicionais para funcionalidades específicas de frontend, backend, API ou banco de dados"],"ru":["Требует четких запросов пользователя для реализации или построения конкретных функций или систем","Может потребовать дополнительных инструментов или библиотек для конкретных функциональностей frontend, backend, API или базы данных"],"ar":["يتطلب طلبات مستخدم واضحة لتنفيذ أو بناء ميزات أو أنظمة محددة","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى أدوات أو مكتبات إضافية لميزات محددة من الجانب الأمامي والجانب الخلفي و API وقاعدة البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"02801f1a80fd63149061e5923ed18375f5d9f1c42d9270f34316f8c27b66f6ea","qualityScore":45}');
