企业级视觉无头内容管理系统，提供GraphQL、Java和开源等特点，帮助开发者高效管理内容","ja":"triageはエンタープライズ向けのビジュアルヘッドレスコンテンツ管理システムで、GraphQL、Java、オープンソースなどを搭載し、開発者のコンテンツ管理を効率化","ko":"triage는 기업용 시각적 헤드리스 콘텐츠 관리 시스템으로 GraphQL, Java, 오픈소스 등의 기능을 제공하여 개발者の 콘텐츠 관리를 효율화합니다","es":"El sistema de gestión de contenido visual headless para empresas ofrece una solución escalable y flexible","fr":"Le système de gestion de contenu headless pour les entreprises offre une solution évolutique et flexible","de":"Das headless Content Management System für Unternehmen bietet eine skalierbare und flexible Lösung","pt":"O triage é um sistema de gerenciamento de conteúdo headless para empresas, oferecendo recursos avançados como GraphQL e CMS.","ru":"Triage - визуальная головоломка для предприятий, предлагающая передовые функции, такие как GraphQL и CMS.","ar":"triage نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس للمؤسسات، يقدم ميزات متقدمة مثل GraphQL و CMS.","en":"The Visual Headless Content Management System for Enterprises"},"definition":{"en":"The Visual Headless Content Management System for Enterprises"},"features":{"zh":["视觉化的内容管理界面","GraphQL支持","基于Java的架构","开源和可扩展","支持多种内容格式"],"ja":["ビジュアルなコンテンツ管理インターフェース","GraphQLサポート","Javaベースのアーキテクチャ","オープンソース且つ拡張可能","多種コンテンツフォーマットのサポート"],"ko":["시각적인 콘텐츠 관리 인터페이스","GraphQL 지원","Java 기반의 아키텍처","오픈소스 및 확장 가능","다양한 콘텐츠 형식 지원"],"es":["Arquitectura headless para una mayor flexibilidad","Soporte para GraphQL y otras tecnologías de API","Desarrollo de aplicaciones personalizadas con Java","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como DotCMS","Escalabilidad y flexibilidad para empresas de todos los tamaños"],"fr":["Architecture headless pour une plus grande flexibilité","Prise en charge de GraphQL et d''autres technologies d''API","Développement d''applications personnalisées avec Java","Intégration avec des outils de développement tels que DotCMS","Évolutivité et flexibilité pour les entreprises de toutes tailles"],"de":["Headless-Architektur für eine größere Flexibilität","Unterstützung für GraphQL und andere API-Technologien","Entwicklung von benutzerdefinierten Anwendungen mit Java","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie DotCMS","Skalierbarkeit und Flexibilität für Unternehmen aller Größen"],"pt":["Sistema de gerenciamento de conteúdo headless","Suporte a GraphQL","Integração com CMS","Plataforma de nuvem","Código aberto"],"ru":["Визуальная головоломка для предприятий","Поддержка GraphQL","Интеграция с CMS","Облачная платформа","Открытый код"],"ar":["نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس","دعم GraphQL","تكامل مع CMS","منصة سحابية","كود مفتوح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用triage","什么是视觉无头内容管理系统","triage替代品","triage与其他CMS的比较","triage安装指南","triage设置教程","GraphQL在triage中的应用","Java开发triage"],"ja":["triageの使い方","ビジュアルヘッドレスコンテンツ管理システムとは","triageの代替","triageと他のCMSの比較","triageのインストールガイド","triageの設定方法","GraphQLをtriageで使用する","Javaでtriageを開発する"],"ko":["triage 사용 방법","시각적 헤드리스 콘텐츠 관리 시스템이란","triage 대체품","triage와 다른 CMS 비교","triage 설치 가이드","triage 설정 방법","GraphQL을 triage에서 사용하는 방법","Java로 triage 개발하기"],"es":["herramientas de triage AI","sistema de gestión de contenido headless","GraphQL para desarrolladores","cómo usar DotCMS","alternativas a DotCMS","instalación de Java para desarrolladores","guía de configuración de GraphQL"],"fr":["outils d''agent de triage","système de gestion de contenu headless","GraphQL pour les développeurs","comment utiliser DotCMS","alternatives à DotCMS","installation de Java pour les développeurs","guide de configuration de GraphQL"],"de":["AI-Triage-Tools","headless Content Management System","GraphQL für Entwickler","wie man DotCMS verwendet","Alternativen zu DotCMS","Java-Installation für Entwickler","GraphQL-Konfigurationshandbuch"],"pt":["como usar triage","o que é sistema de gerenciamento de conteúdo headless","triage vs dotcms","instalar triage","guias de configuração do triage","alternativas ao triage"],"ru":["как использовать triage","что такое визуальная головоломка для предприятий","triage vs dotcms","установить triage","руководства по настройке triage","альтернативы triage"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام triage","ما هو نظام إدارة المحتوى بدون رأس","triage vs dotcms","تثبيت triage","دلائل إعداد triage","بديل triage"]}},"owner":"dotCMS","repo":"core","repoPath":"dotCMS/core","stars":936,"forks":481,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T07:45:00Z","topics":["cloud","cms","content","content-management-system","dotcms","dxp","graphql","headless-cms","java","opensouce"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"triage","description":"Triage GitHub issues using the AI triage pipeline. Fetches the next issue from the Needs Triage project column (or a specific issue), creates an agent team to validate completeness, detect duplicates, and research the codebase in parallel, then presents a triage proposal for human approval before posting anything to GitHub.","bodyPreview":"# AI Issue Triage\n\nYou are now the triage orchestrator. Follow these steps exactly.\n\n## Step 1: Environment check\n\nRun these checks. Stop with an error message if any fail:\n```bash\ngh --version\ngh auth status\ngh repo view --json nameWithOwner --jq ''.nameWithOwner''\n```\nThe repo must be `dotCMS/core`. If not, stop and tell the user to run this from the repo root.\n\n## Step 2: Parse arguments and get issue number\n\nArguments received: `$ARGUMENTS`\n\n**If `--issue <number>` is present**, extract the is","body":"# AI Issue Triage\n\nYou are now the triage orchestrator. Follow these steps exactly.\n\n## Step 1: Environment check\n\nRun these checks. Stop with an error message if any fail:\n```bash\ngh --version\ngh auth status\ngh repo view --json nameWithOwner --jq ''.nameWithOwner''\n```\nThe repo must be `dotCMS/core`. If not, stop and tell the user to run this from the repo root.\n\n## Step 2: Parse arguments and get issue number\n\nArguments received: `$ARGUMENTS`\n\n**If `--issue <number>` is present**, extract the issue number and skip to Step 3.\n\n**If no arguments**, fetch the next issue from the queue:\n```bash\ngh issue list --repo dotCMS/core --search \"is:issue no:assignee -label:\\\"Team : Falcon\\\",\\\"Team : Platform\\\",\\\"Team : Scout\\\",\\\"Team : Maintenance\\\",\\\"Team : Modernization\\\",\\\"Team : Enablement\\\",\\\"Flakey Test\\\" no:parent-issue -linked:pr state:open type:Task,Bug sort:updated-asc\" --json title,number,url --limit 1\n```\n\nExtract the `number` from the first result. If the array is empty, stop and tell the user: \"No issues need triage — queue is empty.\"\n\n## Step 3: Fetch the issue\n\n```bash\ngh issue view <number> --repo dotCMS/core --json number,title,body,labels,assignees,url,projectItems\n```\n\n## Step 4: Pre-flight check\n\nSkip and stop if:\n- Issue has any assignee\n- Issue has any label starting with `Team :`\n- Issue has a parent issue\n\n## Step 5: Create agent team and run three teammates IN PARALLEL\n\n### 5a. Create the team\n\n```\nTeamCreate(team_name: \"triage-<number>\", description: \"Triage pipeline for issue #<number>\")\n```\n\n### 5b. Create the task list\n\nCreate four tasks using `TaskCreate`. The team-router task must be blocked by the code-researcher task.\n\n- Task A: \"Validate issue #<number> completeness\" (assign to validator)\n- Task B: \"Detect duplicates for issue #<number>\" (assign to dup-detector)\n- Task C: \"Research codebase for issue #<number>\" (assign to researcher) — save the task ID\n- Task D: \"Route issue #<number> to team\" (assign to router) — set `addBlockedBy: [Task C ID]`\n\n### 5c. Spawn three teammates in a SINGLE message (parallel)\n\nYou MUST make THREE Task tool calls in a single response. Do not do any research yourself.\n\n**Teammate 1** — `subagent_type: issue-validator`, `team_name: \"triage-<number>\"`, `name: \"validator\"`\nPass the full issue content. Tell it to mark Task A as in_progress, complete it when done, and send results back to you via SendMessage.\n\n**Teammate 2** — `subagent_type: duplicate-detector`, `team_name: \"triage-<number>\"`, `name: \"dup-detector\"`\nPass issue number, title, body, and 3-5 keywords. Tell it to mark Task B as in_progress, complete it when done, and send results back to you via SendMessage.\n\n**Teammate 3** — `subagent_type: code-researcher`, `team_name: \"triage-<number>\"`, `name: \"researcher\"`\nPass issue number, title, full body, inferred type, and repo path (current working directory). Tell it to mark Task C as in_progress, complete it when done, and send results (especially the `Relevant Files` list) back to you via SendMessage.\n\nWait for all three teammates to send their results via SendMessage.\n\n### 5d. Spawn team-router after researcher completes\n\nOnce you receive the researcher''s SendMessage with the `Relevant Files` list, spawn the router teammate:\n\n**Teammate 4** — `subagent_type: team-router`, `team_name: \"triage-<number>\"`, `name: \"router\"`\nPass the `Relevant Files` list from the researcher''s message directly in the prompt. Do not ask it to search for files. Tell it to mark Task D as in_progress, complete it when done, and send the suggested team back to you via SendMessage.\n\nWait for the router to send its result via SendMessage.\n\n### 5e. Shut down teammates and delete team\n\nAfter all four teammates have reported their results:\n\n1. Send `SendMessage(type: \"shutdown_request\")` to all four teammates.\n2. Wait for shutdown confirmations.\n3. Call `TeamDelete()` to clean up the team.\n\n## Step 6: Synthesize and present proposal\n\nCombine the four results into a triage proposal. Use the `Suggested Team` from team-router, complexity from code-researcher.\n\nThe team-router always returns a team — use it as-is. Do not re-check the triage config or do your own routing.\n\nFor priority, map severity to these exact label names:\n- Critical / Show Stopper → `Priority : 1 Show Stopper`\n- High → `Priority : 2 High`\n- Medium / Average → `Priority : 3 Average`\n- Low → `Priority : 4 Low`\n\nShow the full proposal to the user and ask: **Approve? yes / no / edit**\n\n## Step 7: Execute on approval\n\nOn `yes`, run these steps in order:\n\n### 7a. Post the triage comment\n```bash\ngh issue comment <number> --repo dotCMS/core --body \"...\"\n```\n\n### 7b. Add labels (use exact label names from Step 6)\n```bash\ngh issue edit <number> --repo dotCMS/core --add-label \"Team : X\" --add-label \"Priority : X X X\"\n```\n\n### 7c. Add issue to the AI Triage Pipeline project and set status to Triaged\n\nFirst, get the project number from the repo variable:\n```bash\ngh variable get TRIAGE_PROJECT_NUMBER --repo dotCMS/core\n```\n\nThen get the item ID and field metadata using that number:\n```bash\ngh api graphql -f query=''\nquery {\n  organization(login: \"dotCMS\") {\n    projectV2(number: <TRIAGE_PROJECT_NUMBER>) {\n      id\n      fields(first: 20) {\n        nodes {\n          ... on ProjectV2SingleSelectField {\n            id\n            name\n            options { id name }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n      items(first: 5) { nodes { id } }\n    }\n  }\n}''\n```\n\nThen add the issue to the project:\n```bash\ngh api graphql -f query=''\nmutation {\n  addProjectV2ItemById(input: {\n    projectId: \"<project-id>\"\n    contentId: \"<issue-node-id>\"\n  }) {\n    item { id }\n  }\n}''\n```\n\nGet the issue node ID with:\n```bash\ngh issue view <number> --repo dotCMS/core --json id --jq ''.id''\n```\n\nThen set the Status field to \"Triaged\" using the item ID and field/option IDs discovered above:\n```bash\ngh api graphql -f query=''\nmutation {\n  updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue(input: {\n    projectId: \"<project-id>\"\n    itemId: \"<item-id>\"\n    fieldId: \"<status-field-id>\"\n    value: { singleSelectOptionId: \"<triaged-option-id>\" }\n  }) {\n    projectV2Item { id }\n  }\n}''\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:27:14.685Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for GitHub-integrated AI Agents needing automated issue triage and repository management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要自动问题分类和仓库管理功能的GitHub集成AI代理。","ja":"GitHubに統合されたAIエージェントが自動的な課題の分類とリポジトリ管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 문제 분류 및 저장소 관리 기능이 필요한 GitHub 통합 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de AI integrados con GitHub que necesitan capacidades de triage de problemas automatizados y administración de repositorios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA intégrés à GitHub nécessitant des capacités de triage de problèmes automatisées et de gestion de référentiels.","de":"Perfekt für GitHub-integrierte KI-Agents, die automatisierte Fähigkeiten zur Problemtriage und Repository-Verwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA integrados ao GitHub que necessitam de capacidades de triagem de problemas automatizados e gerenciamento de repositórios.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, интегрированных с GitHub, требующих автоматизированной сортировки проблем и возможностей управления репозиторием.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتكاملين مع GitHub الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات إدارة المشكلات والملحقات التلقائية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform environment checks, parse arguments, and extract issue numbers using GitHub CLI commands like `gh --version` and `gh repo view --json`.","zh":"赋予代理执行环境检查、解析参数和使用GitHub CLI命令（如`gh --version`和`gh repo view --json`）提取问题编号的能力。","ja":"エージェントに環境のチェック、引数の解析、およびGitHub CLIコマンド（例： `gh --version`および`gh repo view --json`）を使用して問題番号を抽出する機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 환경을 확인하고, 매개 변수를 분석하고, GitHub CLI 명령어(`gh --version` 및 `gh repo view --json` 같은)를 사용하여 문제 번호를 추출하는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar comprobaciones de entorno, analizar argumentos y extraer números de problema utilizando comandos de GitHub CLI como `gh --version` y `gh repo view --json`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des vérifications d''environnement, d''analyser des arguments et d''extraire des numéros de problème en utilisant des commandes GitHub CLI comme `gh --version` et `gh repo view --json`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Umgebungsprüfungen durchzuführen, Argumente zu parsen und Problemmnummern mithilfe von GitHub CLI-Befehlen wie `gh --version` und `gh repo view --json` zu extrahieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar verificações de ambiente, analisar argumentos e extrair números de problemas usando comandos do GitHub CLI como `gh --version` e `gh repo view --json`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять проверки среды, парсить аргументы и извлекать номера проблем с помощью команд GitHub CLI, таких как `gh --version` и `gh repo view --json`.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء فحوصات بيئية وتحليل الحجج واستخراج أرقام المشكلات باستخدام أوامر GitHub CLI مثل `gh --version` و `gh repo view --json`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating issue triage workflows","Validating repository environments","Extracting issue numbers from command-line arguments"],"zh":["自动化问题分类工作流","验证仓库环境","从命令行参数中提取问题编号"],"ja":["課題の分類ワークフローを自動化する","リポジトリ環境を検証する","コマンドライン引数から問題番号を抽出する"],"ko":["문제 분류 워크플로 자동화","저장소 환경 확인","명령줄 인자로부터 문제 번호 추출"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de triage de problemas","Validación de entornos de repositorio","Extracción de números de problema de argumentos de línea de comandos"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de triage de problèmes","Validation des environnements de référentiel","Extraction des numéros de problème à partir d''arguments de ligne de commande"],"de":["Automatisierung von Problemtriage-Workflows","Validierung von Repository-Umgebungen","Extraktion von Problemmnummern aus Befehlszeilenargumenten"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de triagem de problemas","Validar ambientes de repositório","Extrair números de problemas de argumentos de linha de comando"],"ru":["Автоматизация потоков работы по сортировке проблем","Проверка среды репозитория","Извлечение номеров проблем из аргументов командной строки"],"ar":["تأتمة سير عمل فرز المشكلات","تحقق من بيئة المستودع","استخراج أرقام المشكلات من حجج سطر الأوامر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub CLI installation","Limited to repositories with GitHub CLI access","Must be run from the repository root directory"],"zh":["需要安装GitHub CLI","仅限于具有GitHub CLI访问权限的仓库","必须从仓库根目录运行"],"ja":["GitHub CLIのインストールが必要","GitHub CLIへのアクセス権を持つリポジトリのみ","リポジトリのルートディレクトリから実行する必要がある"],"ko":["GitHub CLI 설치가 필요함","GitHub CLI 접근 권한이 있는 저장소에서만 제한됨","저장소 루트 디렉토리에서 실행되어야 함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de GitHub CLI","Limitado a repositorios con acceso a GitHub CLI","Debe ejecutarse desde el directorio raíz del repositorio"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de GitHub CLI","Limité aux référentiels avec accès à GitHub CLI","Doit être exécuté à partir du répertoire racine du référentiel"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von GitHub CLI","Begrenzt auf Repositorys mit GitHub CLI-Zugriff","Muss aus dem Repository-Stammdirktor ausgeführt werden"],"pt":["Requer instalação do GitHub CLI","Limitado a repositórios com acesso ao GitHub CLI","Deve ser executado a partir do diretório raiz do repositório"],"ru":["Требует установки GitHub CLI","Ограничен репозиториями с доступом к GitHub CLI","Должен быть запущен из корневого каталога репозитория"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت GitHub CLI","محدود بالمستودعات التي لديها وصول إلى GitHub CLI","يجب تشغيله من دليل الجذر للمستودع"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d0655da305e66634744aecb1ea3031d692afa7e7f7c6b89bd875291062995971","qualityScore":44}');
